{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K39BrHterkJ6wGsEArQoao","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# GWL Harness Orchestration Layer (G1+G2) — Execution Log\n2\t\n3\tForeman records per-wave build outcomes below. 6 wave(s) planned (Shark-Tank-refined: verify split into read-only W4 + command-exec W6; replanning W5 decoupled; approval gate W3 added).\n4\t\n5\t## Waves\n6\t\n7\t### Wave 1 — C2 Clarification: the `ask` terminal action — ✅ GREEN (2026-06-12)\n8\t- **EXECUTE:** `step.mjs` (parseDecision +literal `ask`; runStep ask terminal branch; new `sanitizeQuestions`/`renderAskQuestions`), `loop.mjs` (res.done distinguishes `stop.reason:\"ask\"` w/ surfaced questions vs `final_answer`), `prompt.mjs` (exported `CLARIFY_INSTRUCTION`, appended to Tier-2 BP2 only when `GWL_HARNESS_CLARIFY===\"1\"`). New test `clarify-ask.test.mjs` (+10).\n9\t- **GATE (orchestrator-run):** `node --test gwl-t2r-brain/harness/*.test.mjs` → **299/299 pass, 0 fail** (baseline 289 → +10). Artifact `.foreman/wave-1-gate.json`.\n10\t- **REVIEW:** 2 independent fresh-context refute-reviewers → both **GO**, 0 BLOCKER/0 MAJOR (1 non-blocking NIT: empty-questions fallback phrasing). Independently verified: flag-off prefix hash == baseline `2524446b…`; flag-on differs & instruction reaches the wire; anti-laundering holds (strict + known-tool paths); no second model (ask is a pure terminal); no existing test modified.\n11\t- **Invariants:** byte-identical-when-off ✅ · Rule A one-model-per-loop ✅ · anti-laundering ✅ · additive tests ✅.\n12\t\n13\t### Wave 2 — C3 Progress narration: one line per observe (LIVE state) — ✅ GREEN (2026-06-12)\n14\t- **EXECUTE:** new `progress.mjs` (`composeProgressLine` — one bounded single-line status from LIVE `ctx.plan_state` + bounded observe digest; `ProgressLineError` thrashing guard, deterministic single-slice, no loop/recursion; `MAX_PROGRESS_CHARS`=200). `loop.mjs` threads optional `onProgress(line)` at the per-step site, fires once per observe step (`res.observation != null`), no-op when absent. New test `progress-narration.test.mjs` (+12).\n15\t- **GATE (orchestrator-run):** 311/311 → after FIX **312/312** (baseline 299 +13). Artifact `.foreman/wave-2-gate.json`.\n16\t- **REVIEW:** 2 independent refute-reviewers → both **GO**, 0 BLOCKER/0 MAJOR. Independently verified: byte-identical-when-off (full ctx+ledger diff), no Store-A import, single-line + hard-cap (1M-char input bounds, no false-positive), thrashing guard throws on pathological cap, fires only on observe steps (terminal `ask`/`final_answer` + unparseable skipped).\n17\t- **FIX (review NIT-1, both reviewers pre-endorsed):** wrap the `onProgress` call in try/catch so a THROWING sink can never convert a run into `abort` — enforces \"observability never alters control flow\". +1 regression test (13 in file).\n18\t- **Invariants:** byte-identical-when-off ✅ · LIVE-state-only (no Store-A) ✅ · Rule A / ledger untouched ✅ · additive tests ✅.\n19\t\n20\t### Wave 3 — C2b Irreversible-tool approval gate (hard act-boundary stop) — ✅ GREEN (2026-06-12)\n21\t- **EXECUTE:** `step.mjs` act-boundary gate `3c-bis` (AFTER provenance, BEFORE `issuedCalls.add`/`runTool`): a `needs_approval` tool consults injected `approvalResolver` (`approve`=one-shot, `always`=sticky via `ctx.approvals`, `deny`=`surface()` `approval_denied` without poisoning `issuedCalls`); NO resolver → terminal pause `ctx.stop.reason:\"approval\"` with `request:{tool,params}` + clean `finalAnswer`. `loop.mjs`: `approvalGateEnabled()` (env `GWL_HARNESS_APPROVAL`), env-gated `needsApproval` set + turn-scoped `approvals` in `makeContext`, `runLoop` args + deps wiring, approval terminal distinct from `ask`/`final_answer`. New test `approval-gate.test.mjs` (+7).\n22\t- **GATE (orchestrator-run):** **319/319 pass** (baseline 312 +7). Artifact `.foreman/wave-3-gate.json`.\n23\t- **REVIEW:** 2 independent refute-reviewers → both **GO**, 0 findings any severity. Independently probed: flag-off byte-identical (resolver 0×, real caller passes neither arg); gate strictly after repeat/sensitive/provenance (`.env` + invented locator rejected first); deny doesn't poison `issuedCalls` (deny→approve retry runs); `always` turn-scoped, no cross-loop leak; terminal `stop.request` surfaced, no raw-JSON leak; no prefix change; no model call; legacy-ctx optional-chaining safe.\n24\t- **Invariants:** default-OFF byte-identical ✅ · no prompt/prefix change ✅ · hard gate after soft guards ✅ · Rule A / ledger untouched ✅ · additive tests ✅.\n25\t\n26\t### Wave 4 — C6a Verify worker (read-only ground truth) — ✅ GREEN (2026-06-12)\n27\t- **EXECUTE:** new `verify.mjs` (`verifyGateEnabled()` env `GWL_HARNESS_VERIFY`; `verifyGate(ctx)` biased OFF on trivial turn / no write-claims; `collectWriteClaims` scans `ctx.history` write actions via WRITE_FS/WRITE_PATH_PARAMS, last-claim-per-path; `runVerify(ctx,deps)` re-reads each claim via an INJECTED reader, deterministic compare, returns `{passed, evidence}` = AND over claims; ZERO model/subprocess calls; books truthful $0 cost into `ctx.usage.verify`). `loop.mjs` post-loop hook (after graceful-final, before `writeAccounting`) runs only when flag+gate pass, attaches `verify` to the return + ctx (OMITTED when not run), reader-fault swallowed. New test `verify-worker.test.mjs` (+17).\n28\t- **GATE (orchestrator-run):** **336/336 pass** (baseline 319 +17). Artifact `.foreman/wave-4-gate.json`.\n29\t- **REVIEW:** 2 independent refute-reviewers → both **GO**, 0 BLOCKER/MAJOR/MINOR. Independently probed: flag-off byte-identical (reader 0×, no `verify` field, ledger keys unchanged, `writeAccounting` never reads verify); no model/subprocess (grep + throwing-clients injection); compare AND-correct (missing/mismatch→false, last-write dedupe, no false-pass); reader-fault never aborts; cost isolated from wallet/envelope; prompt/prefix untouched. NITs (non-blocking): substring-containment is intentional, edit_file param convention runtime-injected.\n30\t- **Invariants:** default-OFF byte-identical ✅ · read-only / no subprocess / no model ✅ · no prompt/prefix change ✅ · Rule A / ledger untouched ✅ · additive tests ✅.\n31\t\n32\t### Wave 5 — Replanning triggers: outer-loop strategy reset (existing signals) — ✅ GREEN (2026-06-12)\n33\t- **EXECUTE:** new `replan.mjs` ONLY (loop/step/prompt UNTOUCHED — outer-loop-only lock honored structurally). `replanEnabled()` env `GWL_HARNESS_REPLAN`; `detectReplanSignal(result)` triggers on `stop.reason===\"no_progress\"` OR `verify.passed===false`, composing the hint from in-loop surfaces (`unverified_locator`>`repeat_call`>`unknown_tool`); `buildRevisedTask` appends a delimited `[REVISED APPROACH n]` block; `runWithReplan(args,opts)` re-invokes the WHOLE loop (fresh runId `${runId}-replanN`, own prefix + own truthful ledger row — `subagent.mjs` precedent), bounded by `MAX_REPLANS_PER_TURN` (default 1, clamped). New test `replan.test.mjs` (+8).\n34\t- **GATE (orchestrator-run):** **344/344 pass** (baseline 336 +8). Purely additive: 2 new files, 0 modified source. Artifact `.foreman/wave-5-gate.json`.\n35\t- **REVIEW:** 2 independent refute-reviewers → both **GO**, 0 BLOCKER/MAJOR/MINOR. Independently probed: loop/step/prompt byte-untouched; flag-off single call returns the unchanged object (task not mutated); bounded across `maxReplans` ∈ {0,1,3,5,-1,2.5,NaN,null,Infinity,\"abc\"} (always `1+clamp`, never runaway); triggers ONLY on no_progress + verify-fail (14-stop-reason matrix, no over-trigger); hint shaped by surfaces; fresh runId, args never corrupted. NITs (non-blocking/intentional): flag-ON stamps `replans:0`; not yet wired to an entrypoint (plumbing-ready, like W3/W4).\n36\t- **Invariants:** outer-loop only (no in-loop seam) ✅ · default-OFF byte-identical ✅ · bounded (never infinite) ✅ · Rule A per re-invoke / truthful per-loop ledger ✅ · additive tests ✅.\n37\t\n38\t### Wave 6 — C6b Command-execution verify (bounded subprocess sandbox) — ✅ GREEN (2026-06-12)\n39\t- **EXECUTE:** new `command-runner.mjs` — the REAL subprocess guard (NOT the path-allowlist): guards IN ORDER argv-only (shell STRING rejected, `shell:false`) → command allowlist (default-deny on argv[0]) → cwd bound under allowRoots (`..`-rejected, segment-prefix so sibling-prefix can't escape) → scrubbed default-deny env (secrets + code-injection vectors stripped) → spawn under a hard timeout that KILLS (best-effort `taskkill /T /F`) and ALWAYS settles the promise. INJECTED `spawnImpl` (no real shell in tests). `verify.mjs` extended: `runCommandVerify` folds the test-command result into `{passed, evidence}` (overall = read-only AND command-check), double-flag-gated (VERIFY+APPROVAL) + W3-authorized (sticky grant or resolver approve/always); deny/no-auth/throwing-resolver/guard-reject all fail safe to not-invoked / passed:false. `loop.mjs` threads `commandRunner`/`testCommand`/`commandVerifyCwd` (default undefined → W4 byte-identical) + registers the runner in needsApproval (env-gated). Runner in NO default tool list → prefix untouched. New test `command-verify.test.mjs` (+22→+23 post-fix).\n40\t- **GATE (orchestrator-run):** 366/366 → after FIX **367/367 pass** (baseline 344 +23). Artifact `.foreman/wave-6-gate.json`.\n41\t- **REVIEW:** 2 independent SECURITY refute-reviewers → both **GO**, 0 BLOCKER/MAJOR. Attacks repelled (stubbed spawn, 0 real shells): shell-injection, argv type-confusion, allowlist bypass, cwd sibling-prefix escape, env-leak, hang (incl. throwing kill seam), gating bypass (APPROVAL off / deny / throwing / no-grant), false-PASS fold, byte-identical-when-off.\n42\t- **FIX (review ≥2-agree MINOR):** hardened `SECRET_ENV_RE` to also strip `NODE_OPTIONS` (=`--require` RCE into a node child), `NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS`, `*_PROXY`, `DATABASE_URL`/`CONNECTION_STRING`/`*_URL`, `PASSPHRASE`/`BEARER`/`AUTH`, `NPM_CONFIG_*` when an operator overrides `envAllowlist`; corrected the overstated comment; +1 regression test (verified strips all vectors, keeps benign keys). Basename-only allowlist left as documented by-design (not exploitable: `testCommand` is caller-config, not model-supplied; runner not in any default tool list).\n43\t- **Invariants:** both-flags-off byte-identical ✅ · every guard rejection spawns 0 processes ✅ · argv-only/allowlist/cwd-bound/env-scrub/timeout-kill each tested ✅ · W3-gated, no prompt/prefix change, Rule A (no model call) ✅ · additive tests ✅.\n44\t\n45\t---\n46\t\n47\t## Project DONE — all 6 waves GREEN (2026-06-12)\n48\tG1+G2 orchestration layer shipped: 6 contiguous waves, each default-OFF + flag/callback-gated, byte-identical when off, every locked invariant preserved (byte-stable BP1/BP2 prefix, one-cache-stable-model-per-loop, truthful once-per-turn ledger, intact rollback). Test gate **289 → 367** (+78), 0 fail. Every wave passed 2 independent fresh-context adversarial refute-reviewers (BLOCKER = ≥2 agree); 0 BLOCKER across the build; W2 + W6 each took one reviewer-driven FIX. Follow-on G3/G4/G5 remain sketched for a later Crucible run.\n49\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01R7onNqhV8BYzhXq32rMA1B","session_id":"75eda862-34e1-4a42-a5f6-73eb4ef1cd9a","uuid":"245b1b0b-25f7-4389-83bd-c058bd8da64b","timestamp":"2026-06-23T18:17:40.977Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Ground Gandalf diagnosis of Agentic-Home"}
