{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E6riYusRcSFtK221JhayyJ","type":"tool_result","content":"Agentic Systems Build Guide.md:96:- `~/.openclaw/agents/<agentId>/workspace/SOUL.md` — persona, rules, style\nAgentic Systems Build Guide.md:97:- `~/.openclaw/agents/<agentId>/workspace/AGENTS.md` — metadata about this agent\nAgentic Systems Build Guide.md:98:- `~/.openclaw/agents/<agentId>/workspace/TOOLS.md` — tool allowlist\nAgentic Systems Build Guide.md:101:Multiple agents can live on one Gateway, or one each on separate machines. The isolation model is strict: every agent has its own workspace, auth directory, and session store.\nAgentic Systems Build Guide.md:199:This creates `~/.openclaw/agents/coder/workspace/`. Edit `SOUL.md`:\nAgentic Systems Build Guide.md:217:Edit `~/.openclaw/agents/writer/workspace/SOUL.md`:\nAgentic Systems Build Guide.md:286:node ~/.openclaw/workspace/plugins/a2a-gateway/skill/scripts/a2a-send.mjs \\\nADDENDUM-P11.5-Source-Aptness-and-Watcher-Memory.md:118:workspace at C:\\Users\\jcl12\\OneDrive - Axmra\\NextGen\\Agentic Home.\nADDENDUM-P11.5-Source-Aptness-and-Watcher-Memory.md:997:2. **Pre-call gate:** `question-quality-check` expert runs *after* Frontal makes a cloud-frontier call (expensive, wasteful). It should run *before* the call to gate vague/template-bound queries and bounce them back to Frontal for re-prompt construction.\nADDENDUM-P11.5-Source-Aptness-and-Watcher-Memory.md:1037:   Before dispatching to Frontal for cloud-frontier calls, inject a\nADDENDUM-P11.5-Source-Aptness-and-Watcher-Memory.md:1071:# Run from workspace root. Requires all P11.5.1-8 implementations.\nACTION-PLAN-Hillsdale-and-Curriculum-2026-05-03.md:262:from PowerShell at the workspace root. If any look real (not redundant),\n.gitignore:19:# - gbrain/ : workspace-root slot RESERVED for Tan's GBrain install (S1 day-5 / 5/19-5/20). Ignored wholesale.\n.gitignore:21:# - gwl-runtime/ : workspace-root runtime state, reserved per v5 §Q-M (moot today; dir may never materialize).\n.gitignore:22:# - C:\\Users\\john\\gwl-corpus\\ (user-profile training-data root, formerly ~/gbrain/) is OUTSIDE the workspace so no gitignore entry is needed.\n.claude_md.tmp.5:3:This file orients any Claude Code (or other coding-agent) session opened at the workspace root. Read it first.\n.claude_md.tmp.5:5:## Canonical workspace location (updated 2026-05-02)\n.claude_md.tmp.5:7:[Omitted long matching line]\n.claude_md.tmp.5:11:## What this workspace is\n.claude_md.tmp.5:13:John Liechty's **Agentic Sandbox** — a research workspace for building, training, and evaluating clusters of AI agents. The active deliverable is the **Ghost World Labs (GWL-M)** master GUI, a Next.js app (`sandbox-lab-gui/`) that launches and supervises agents running on the **OpenClaw** runtime (MIT-licensed, installed globally via npm).\n.claude_md.tmp.5:26:Entry point: `Launch-Ghost-World-Labs.bat` at the workspace root.\n.claude_md.tmp.5:32:3. `server.mjs` reads `../.env` (the workspace-root `.env`) to inherit `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` and `GEMINI_API_KEY`. **It re-reads `.env` on every PTY spawn, so a key saved through the Settings Vault takes effect on the next terminal launch — no server restart needed.**\n.claude_md.tmp.5:46:| **The Alpha Agent and every other agent launched from the GUI** | **API keys** — `GEMINI_API_KEY` for Google providers, `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` for Anthropic providers. Stored in the workspace `.env`, edited via the Settings Vault. |\n.claude_md.tmp.5:56:- `alpha` — The Architect. Gemini (`google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview` per current routing). PVB cognitive architecture. Persona source-of-truth at `Sandbox Setup Package/PERSONAS/global/alpha-personal-manager.md`. OpenClaw runtime copies live at `~/.openclaw/agents/alpha/SOUL.md` (workspace root) and `~/.openclaw/agents/alpha/agent/SOUL.md`. Five skills declared in YAML frontmatter: `deep-think`, `deep-research`, `expert-coder`, `agent-builder`, `curriculum-builder`.\n.claude_md.tmp.5:58:- `prime-coder` — Codes the GUI and harness scripts. Anthropic (`claude-opus-4-7`), 16k token budget.\n.claude_md.tmp.5:74:`Bootstrap-Agentic-Home.ps1` runs this for you (after the workspace has been cloned/copied to `C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home`). After install, `~/.openclaw/` exists with `agents/`, `skills/`, `plugins/`, and `openclaw.json`.\n.claude_md.tmp.5:113:**Diagnostic order when it hangs again** (so the next iteration takes 10 minutes, not 3 days):\n.claude_md.tmp.5:185:This workspace uses a master skill repository linked into Claude Code, Gemini CLI, and (via copy) OpenClaw. The link strategies differ by tool:\n.claude_md.tmp.5:207:The workspace root has ~80 markdown files. Important ones grouped by purpose:\n.claude_md.tmp.5:221:- `.env` at the workspace root — gitignored; contains real API keys. Do not commit. Do not echo. Do not paste into messages.\n.claude_md.tmp.5:237:All logs live under `logs/` at the workspace root (gitignored). When the user reports a crash or unexpected behavior, read these *before* asking them to copy-paste from the terminal:\n.claude_md.tmp.5:258:From the workspace root, in PowerShell:\n.claude_md.tmp.5:274:[Omitted long matching line]\n.claude_md.tmp.5:277:[Omitted long matching line]\n.claude_md.tmp.5:281:- 2026-04-28: First Alpha workspace bootstrap created at `~/.openclaw/agents/alpha/`.\nAll-Agent Virtual Conference — Dean Proposal.md:20:[Omitted long matching line]\nAll-Agent Virtual Conference — Dean Proposal.md:52:[Omitted long matching line]\nARCHITECTURE-Alpha-Agent-Brain-v2.md:11:5. **A local-LLM substrate is added.** Small open-source models served on localhost (Ollama in dev, vLLM in production) for the fast/cheap regions. The Frontal still calls cloud frontier models. OpenClaw gains a model-serve harness so agent code is identical regardless of where the model runs.\nARCHITECTURE-Alpha-Agent-Brain-v2.md:29:**(e) Cloud LLMs for inner-brain regions are wrong on both timing and cost.** Sensory dispatching a Read shouldn't require a 600 ms round-trip to Anthropic. Watcher checking a citation shouldn't either. We need a localhost LLM service for the fast regions, with a clean abstraction so the same agent code runs against laptop-grade models in dev (Ollama serving Qwen-2.5-1.5B) and workstation-grade models in production (vLLM serving Qwen-3-7B or Phi-4 14B in 4-bit). §7 specifies that substrate.\nARCHITECTURE-Alpha-Agent-Brain-v2.md:91:              |   cloud frontier | none)           |\nARCHITECTURE-Alpha-Agent-Brain-v2.md:135:3. **Active context** (workspace + recent envelopes). The current turn's plan, sub-goals, open-questions, and the previous N envelopes on the bus. *What's going on right now.*\nARCHITECTURE-Alpha-Agent-Brain-v2.md:142:This is the cheapest possible MoE — no learned gate weights, no separate gate model. It works because the embedder (`all-MiniLM-L6-v2`, 384-d, ~30ms on CPU) is already good enough to recognize the *kind* of input, and skills have descriptive text that says what they're for.\nARCHITECTURE-Alpha-Agent-Brain-v2.md:173:- **The active workspace** is not a memory — it's working state, cleared at session end.\nARCHITECTURE-Alpha-Agent-Brain-v2.md:245:**Provider/model.** Local-LLM 3-7B for relevance scoring; embedding is local sentence-transformers. The frontier model is never called from Hippocampus.\nARCHITECTURE-Alpha-Agent-Brain-v2.md:265:**Experts.** `plan`, `critique`, `integrate`, `decide-when-stuck`. Each maps to a frontier-model call shape with a specific output schema.\nARCHITECTURE-Alpha-Agent-Brain-v2.md:267:**Local memory.** `active/workspace.json` — goals, sub-goals, hypotheses, open-questions, contradictions, budget-state. Cleared at session start.\nARCHITECTURE-Alpha-Agent-Brain-v2.md:269:**Provider/model.** Cloud frontier model (Gemini 3.1 Pro for Alpha today; Claude Opus 4.6 for some workloads). The only region that pays for slow-think.\nARCHITECTURE-Alpha-Agent-Brain-v2.md:296:**Experts.** `calibration-check`, `confabulation-check`, `budget-check`, `coherence-check` (new — does the integrate output contradict an earlier turn in this session?), `style-check` (new — is the output drifting from persona conventions?), `question-quality-check` (added in the 2026-04-30 PM amendment — see §14: is the prompt to the cloud frontier model sharp, well-framed, and worth its tokens? Runs *before* the cloud call, not after).\nARCHITECTURE-Alpha-Agent-Brain-v2.md:366:    workspace.json                   # Frontal's working memory\nARCHITECTURE-Alpha-Agent-Brain-v2.md:412:Piaget's developmental account distinguishes *assimilation* (fitting new evidence into existing schemas) from *accommodation* (revising schemas under pressure from new evidence). A live agent does assimilation in every turn — the Frontal-INTEGRATE absorbs new evidence into the workspace. Accommodation needs *time and replay*. That's what sleep is for.\nARCHITECTURE-Alpha-Agent-Brain-v2.md:470:     L_frontier_leverage = mean(grade) / mean(cloud_frontier_tokens_spent)\nARCHITECTURE-Alpha-Agent-Brain-v2.md:477:   substrate). The seventh axis (frontier_leverage) is the\nARCHITECTURE-Alpha-Agent-Brain-v2.md:545:This matches how cognitive consolidation actually works: routine REM-cycle pruning every night, large structural reorganizations rare and triggered by accumulated stress. It also matches the engineering principle that *big moves are only justified when the model is really off* — small steady drift gets caught by mechanical residual nudges; big structural rethinks happen only when the multi-axis stress signal demands them.\nARCHITECTURE-Alpha-Agent-Brain-v2.md:583:Cell `cell.config.json` then says `\"provider\": \"local\", \"model\": \"qwen-3-7b\"` for the fast regions. No agent code changes when the underlying engine swaps from Ollama (laptop) to vLLM (workstation).\nARCHITECTURE-Alpha-Agent-Brain-v2.md:585:### 7.3 Tier strategy — laptop vs workstation\nARCHITECTURE-Alpha-Agent-Brain-v2.md:589:| Cell | Tier on **laptop** (Ollama) | Tier on **workstation** (vLLM) |\nARCHITECTURE-Alpha-Agent-Brain-v2.md:596:| Consolidator (dream judge) | cloud frontier | cloud frontier |\nARCHITECTURE-Alpha-Agent-Brain-v2.md:597:| Frontal | cloud frontier (Gemini 3.1 Pro / Claude Opus) | cloud frontier (same) |\nARCHITECTURE-Alpha-Agent-Brain-v2.md:599:Phi-4 14B is reserved for cells where reasoning quality matters more than latency, on the workstation tier — currently the Librarian's `manifest-by-domain` and the Consolidator's `skill-edit-propose`.\nARCHITECTURE-Alpha-Agent-Brain-v2.md:618:- **vLLM** wins on throughput at concurrency. Once the workstation is hosting Alpha + Sigma + Prime Coder + watchers in parallel (Phase 7 of master plan), vLLM's PagedAttention gives ~6x the total throughput at p99 latency under 3 seconds vs Ollama's ~25 s. That's the difference between agents thinking simultaneously and agents queueing.\n\n[Showing results with pagination = limit: 60]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01R7onNqhV8BYzhXq32rMA1B","session_id":"75eda862-34e1-4a42-a5f6-73eb4ef1cd9a","uuid":"1d1cef5a-7ed5-4d9e-a97f-923a4b0123d7","timestamp":"2026-06-23T18:17:57.082Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Ground Gandalf diagnosis of Agentic-Home"}
