{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UEbHA3MsefkKqJZDxZE7e8","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Costs — Budgeting and Kill Switches\n2\t\n3\tThis document covers where the money goes, how Alpha tracks it, and what happens automatically when the system starts spending too fast.\n4\t\n5\t## Where cost comes from\n6\t\n7\tThe sandbox has three sources of paid spend:\n8\t\n9\t1. **Anthropic API** — most of the cost. Every token sent to Claude Opus/Sonnet/Haiku is billed. This is separate from Claude Max subscription; Claude Max covers chat on `claude.ai`, not programmatic API use.\n10\t2. **Google Gemini API** — used by S01 (paper finder) and optionally W01 (research) via Gemini 2.x Pro for cheaper long-context reading. Separate from Gemini Ultra consumer subscription.\n11\t3. **Electricity + hardware depreciation** — real but not budgeted here; the $5k workstation and the power it draws are one-time and treated as fixed.\n12\t\n13\tLocal inference (Llama, Mistral, etc. via Ollama) is optional and is free at the margin; if John adopts local inference for the Haiku-tier roles it reduces spend significantly. See \"Local inference\" below.\n14\t\n15\t## The three budget caps\n16\t\n17\tConfigured in INSTALL.md §8. Values are defaults — tune as patterns emerge.\n18\t\n19\t| Cap | Default | Enforcement |\n20\t|--|--|--|\n21\t| `limits.per_task_usd` | $1.00 | A single A2A task that projects to exceed this amount aborts and reports. |\n22\t| `limits.per_day_usd` | $20.00 | When today's spend hits this, all non-Alpha agents are paused. Alpha can still run and talk to John. |\n23\t| `limits.per_month_usd` | $200.00 | When month-to-date hits this, all agents pause, including Alpha's proactive pulses (but Alpha remains reachable on demand). |\n24\t\n25\tAlpha's daily digest surfaces today's spend, 7-day trend, and month-to-date relative to the cap.\n26\t\n27\t## Per-agent model routing (drives most of the variance)\n28\t\n29\tDefault routing (see INSTALL.md §7):\n30\t\n31\t- **Opus** — Alpha, W-MANAGER, S-MANAGER. High reasoning, low volume. ~$15 / million input tokens, ~$75 / million output tokens (rough Apr 2026 prices; check current).\n32\t- **Sonnet** — most workers (W04 drafter, S04 coder, S02 method extractor, etc.). Balance of quality and cost. ~$3 / $15.\n33\t- **Haiku** — formatting, fact-checking where claim extraction is mechanical, figure caption writing. ~$0.80 / $4.\n34\t\n35\tA ballpark monthly estimate at medium use:\n36\t\n37\t- ~50 writing briefs × $3 each = $150 (drafting dominates).\n38\t- ~20 scientific briefs × $5 each = $100 (verification + runs dominate).\n39\t- Alpha + Sigma overhead ~$15.\n40\t- Benchmarks $5.\n41\t\n42\tThat's $270 — over the default $200 cap. Options to get under:\n43\t\n44\t- Cut drafter tokens with Sigma's best-practice recommendations.\n45\t- Route more formatters to Haiku.\n46\t- Local inference for W07, W06, S07 (see below).\n47\t- Raise the cap deliberately and accept $300/mo.\n48\t\n49\tAlpha's monthly review is where this conversation happens.\n50\t\n51\t## How Alpha tracks spend\n52\t\n53\tEvery API call produces a usage record. OpenClaw captures these and writes them to `~/.openclaw/usage.jsonl`. Alpha aggregates in three scopes:\n54\t\n55\t- Per-task: sum the usage lines tagged with the task's ID.\n56\t- Per-day: group by `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n57\t- Per-month: group by `YYYY-MM`.\n58\t\n59\tThe pulse (every 30 min) re-aggregates the current day and month and updates `~/gbrain/benchmarks/cost-current.json`.\n60\t\n61\t## Kill switches\n62\t\n63\tWhen a cap trips, the Gateway's cost-enforcement middleware:\n64\t\n65\t1. Rejects new task requests to the affected scope (task / all agents except Alpha / all agents).\n66\t2. Signals Alpha via A2A `budget-breached` event.\n67\t3. Alpha writes an incident and messages John.\n68\t\n69\tTo resume:\n70\t\n71\t- **Intentional resume** — John types \"resume\" in a chat with Alpha. Alpha confirms the current spend and asks whether to raise the cap temporarily (just for this day / month) or permanently.\n72\t- **Next period auto-resume** — at midnight the daily cap resets automatically. The monthly cap resets on day 1.\n73\t\n74\t## Cost spike detection\n75\t\n76\tA cap breach is a symptom; the cause is usually a runaway loop. Alpha also watches for:\n77\t\n78\t- An agent calling the same tool > 20 times in 10 minutes (infinite-loop signature).\n79\t- An A2A thread > 50 messages deep (agents talking past each other).\n80\t- A single prompt > 100k tokens (probably dumped too much context).\n81\t\n82\tIf any fires, Alpha pauses the offending agent *before* the hard cap trips, writes an incident, and asks John what to do.\n83\t\n84\t## Per-project budgets\n85\t\n86\tFor big pieces of work, John can assign a project budget in the BRIEF:\n87\t\n88\t```markdown\n89\tBudget: $10 total, $3 max per sub-task.\n90\t```\n91\t\n92\tThe cluster manager subtracts each task's spend from the project budget and refuses to start a new task once the budget is down to < $0.50 remaining without explicit John reauthorization.\n93\t\n94\t## Local inference — the cost escape hatch\n95\t\n96\tThe RTX 5090 workstation can run local models. Strong candidates for offload:\n97\t\n98\t- **Llama 3.1 70B** (or its 2026 successor) for Haiku-class tasks — line editing, fact-extraction, captions.\n99\t- **Qwen or DeepSeek** coder models for boilerplate S04 tasks where the coder doesn't need the reasoning of Sonnet.\n100\t\n101\tSetup path (not default, but supported):\n102\t\n103\t1. Install Ollama on WSL2 or on the Windows side with a WSL bridge.\n104\t2. Pull the target model.\n105\t3. Update `~/.openclaw/routing.json` to route specific agents to `ollama://...` endpoints.\n106\t4. Test output quality on the monthly benchmark job before trusting it for production.\n107\t\n108\tThe tradeoff is latency (local is slower on these sizes) and quality (local 70B is still behind Sonnet for most tasks). The right move is to start all-API, then offload roles where Sigma's scan shows the quality gap is acceptable.\n109\t\n110\t## What John sees\n111\t\n112\tJohn should look at:\n113\t\n114\t- The daily digest: \"today $4.12 / month $68 / cap $200.\"\n115\t- The monthly retro: \"this month $172, up 8% from last month, driven by S05 runs on the diffusion project.\"\n116\t\n117\tIf spend ever surprises John — either too high or suspiciously too low — he can ask Alpha for a breakdown, and Alpha produces a by-agent cost table from the usage log.\n118\t\n119\t## Cost safety rules that are non-negotiable\n120\t\n121\t- No agent has access to API credentials directly; they call through the Gateway.\n122\t- The Anthropic API key has a usage cap set at Anthropic's dashboard **and** at the Gateway level. Two layers of protection.\n123\t- API keys live in `~/.openclaw/secrets/` with mode `600`, not in `~/gbrain/`, not in git.\n124\t- Raising a monthly cap past $500 is a Tier 3 action (explicit plaintext approval from John each time).\n125\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01R7onNqhV8BYzhXq32rMA1B","session_id":"75eda862-34e1-4a42-a5f6-73eb4ef1cd9a","uuid":"654fc4bd-f19d-4aa0-82f9-84b6846d893e","timestamp":"2026-06-23T18:18:01.225Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Ground Gandalf diagnosis of Agentic-Home"}
