{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018UyKA5ebd8pefHW43au9rd","type":"tool_result","content":"C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home/docs/plans/PLAN-Sovereign-T2R-Harness-Implementation-v2.md:**Through-line (Architect):** cache-stability — correctly discovered — silently demotes three marquee gold-standard features (per-step tiering, per-step skill selection, per-step local savings) from \"per-step\" to \"loop-scoped or unvalidated.\" The architecture is sound; the *claims* weren't honest about what cache-stability costs. v2 fixes the claims, the two P0 bugs, and gates the spend.\nC:\\dev\\Agentic-Home/docs/plans/PLAN-Sovereign-T2R-Harness-Implementation-v2.md:A rigorous flaw-hunt on the gold standard and the plan found the architecture sound but the *case* over-claimed: the headline −56% rests on an unvalidated local-model competence bet (prior art ⇒ realistic ~−30–35%, much of it capturable by extending OpenClaw), \"tier every step\" is really loop-locked, and there are two P0 correctness bugs (lossy one-way compression; a broken no-progress metric). v2 **gates the entire build behind a 1-day spike** with a three-way go/no-go (raw gateway / extend-OpenClaw-compression / harness) — build the harness only if local sub-decisions clear ~85% success and beat the *extend* baseline by a margin worth the rebuild; otherwise ship the compression inside an OpenClaw plugin. It also fixes the P0/P1 defects: a `read_raw` affordance + extractive compression, a plan-state progress counter, a tail budget, a normalized hash + `resetCache`, and side-effect idempotency. Everything else (two layers, cache discipline, bounded loop, POD-debug-state, reuse, feature-flag cutover) carries forward. **Recommended next action: run the Phase-0 spike — it decides whether to build at all.**","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01R7onNqhV8BYzhXq32rMA1B","session_id":"75eda862-34e1-4a42-a5f6-73eb4ef1cd9a","uuid":"542ed907-be87-4a6f-8d5e-7a0097f3d525","timestamp":"2026-06-23T18:18:03.869Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Ground Gandalf diagnosis of Agentic-Home"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HmNVGW5BrETVYQSWVWMudJ","type":"tool_result","content":"C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home/ADDENDUM-P11.5-Source-Aptness-and-Watcher-Memory.md:**Why this matters.** The Watcher is specified as \"always on, mostly silent, ready to interrupt when the narrow path has lost the plot\" (ARCHITECTURE v2 §3.6). Without a memory of its own firings, it cannot spot *patterns* across turns — repeated mistakes, recurring ignored signals, systematic blind spots. These patterns are the attentional equivalent of semantic shards: discoveries the Watcher has made that deserve to be consolidated into procedural or semantic memory.\nC:\\dev\\Agentic-Home/ADDENDUM-P11.5-Source-Aptness-and-Watcher-Memory.md:  - \"Are there any systematic blind spots in the Frontal's reasoning?\"\nC:\\dev\\Agentic-Home/CLAUDE.md:- **2026-05-28/29 — Sovereign t2r Harness: M0 built + hardened + independently validated; M1 planned.** Built M0 (clean ReAct loop the agent owns; ONE cache-stable remote model per loop; guarded decision prompt; one MCP filesystem tool; 4 bounded-loop guards + code provenance arg-validator + secret-file deny-list; truthful per-turn ledger; `ecgberht` pilot behind `GWL_HARNESS_AGENTS`, gateway client = instant rollback) — acceptance gate GREEN (cache invariant + cost win live-verified). Built + validated via the **Swarm Sandwich** (design-swarm -> solo build -> validation-swarm): the M0 validation swarm caught+fixed F1 (stream-stall hang)/F2 (wallet-cap not threaded)/F3 (secret deny-list); the M1 **hardening backlog** landed 13 robustness fixes; an **independent adversarial review** then found+fixed 2 P0s all three swarms missed (mid-stream double-bill + $0-ledger from Anthropic deferring `output_tokens` to `message_delta`; a client-craftable `alpha-v0`->harness routing leak). harness 43 + brain 61 tests green; 5-turn live soak clean. Code in `gwl-t2r-brain/harness/` + `sandbox-lab-gui/agent-chat-v0-harness.mjs`; branch `feat/guarded-rightsize-routing` (commits `ca227113`..`2d50ae1e`, pushed; PR HELD — branch carries a 193-file nightly snapshot + prior t2r-v2.1 work the harness depends on). **M1 FEATURE plan** (provider portability incl. Gemini/OpenAI/Grok cache adapters [today only Anthropic has the cache cost-win], MCP fleet+supervisor, read_raw, moving history breakpoint, hybrid compression, warmth promoter, episodic memory) in `PLAN-M1-Build-2026-05-29.md`. Reports: `REPORT-M0-SWARM-VALIDATION.md`, `REPORT-M1-Hardening-2026-05-29.md`, `REPORT-INDEPENDENT-VALIDATION.md`. The Swarm Sandwich strategy is codified in `expert-coder/SKILL.md`.\nC:\\dev\\Agentic-Home/CLAUDE_hist.md:- **2026-05-25 (round 2) — t2r v2.1: docs-verified pricing (Aurora was WRONG) + local model as the $0 lowest tier.** (1) **Pricing corrected to Anthropic's official docs** (`platform.claude.com/docs/.../pricing`): **Opus 4.5/4.6/4.7 = $5/$25** (the $15/$75 is *deprecated* Opus 4.1); **Haiku 4.5 = $1/$5** ($0.8/$4 is *retired* Haiku 3.5); Sonnet 4.6 $3/$15. **Aurora's `pricing.yaml` was wrong** — it pinned the deprecated/retired prices onto the current models; its nightly LLM judge (`C:\\dev\\aurora\\roles\\pricing_collector.py`) adjudicated backwards (chose $15/$75 over the correct $5/$25) and **will revert its file nightly until fixed.** So Aurora is **demoted to advisory**: `taste.mjs` resolution is now `openclaw.json → Aurora → hardcoded`, all three set to docs values; `~/.openclaw/openclaw.json` restored to $5/$25 + $1/$5 (backup `.bak-pricing-2026-05-25`). Verified: 7/7 units (Opus 1M+1M=$30, Haiku=$6, cache 0.5/6.25) + live sonnet turn $0.040156 = exact recompute. (2) **Trivial reasoning tier → local ($0)** — `ollama/qwen2.5:7b-instruct-q4_K_M` (NOT llama3, which 400s \"does not support tools\" since OpenClaw sends tool schemas every turn). Verified live: \"hi\"→ollama/qwen2.5, real reply, ledger reasoning=$0; coding→sonnet (escalation intact). (3) Local caching = latency only (`keep_alive=-1`: cold ~2