{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013sP2rqqBUn1KRGwiSY3r57","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# GWL t2r Brain — Execution Log\n2\t\n3\tForeman records per-wave build outcomes below. 7 wave(s) planned.\n4\t\n5\t## Waves\n6\t\n7\t### Wave 1 — E1 Brain-seam contract (+ baseline & sovereign controls) — ✅ GREEN\n8\t\n9\t- **Built:** `gwl-t2r-brain/harness/brain-seam.mjs` (documented `pickLock`/`reason`/`compress` seam, `isBrain` validator, `makeOpusBaselineBrain` [D5], `makeSovereignBrain` [D6, structural local-only deny via `assertLocalModel`], `runLoopWithBrain` wrapping the real `runLoop` — no fork) + `gwl-t2r-brain/harness/brain-seam.test.mjs` (7 conformance tests, offline/injected-fake transport).\n10\t- **Given-When-Then:** (a) Opus-4.8 brain → loop completes; (b) Sovereign brain → loop completes with zero third-party URLs (+ structural deny proven 3 ways); (c) D9 size-agnostic swap (7–8B→72B, Opus→opus-4-8-1m) config-only, still conforms.\n11\t- **Review:** 2 independent refute-reviewers → both GO, zero BLOCKER/MAJOR (2 doc-grade MINOR nits on `providerOf` id-classification + env-overridable `OLLAMA_BASE`; non-blocking).\n12\t- **Gate (orchestrator-run):** `node --test gwl-t2r-brain/harness/*.test.mjs` → **161 pass / 0 fail** (was 154; +7). Converged in 0 fix-iters.\n13\t\n14\t### Wave 2 — E2 Observe gated context-worker — ✅ GREEN\n15\t\n16\t- **Built:** `gwl-t2r-brain/harness/observe-gate.mjs` (pre-Observe gate `observeGate`/`routeToGateTier` → none/local/frontier, reusing F6 `profileOutput`/`routeCompression`; net-savings meter `accObserve`/`newObserveMeter` recording `tokens_saved − observe_cost` per turn) + `observe-gate.test.mjs` (13 tests). Additive edits to `step.mjs` (snapshot frontier spend + `accObserve`), `loop.mjs` (seed `ctx.usage.observe`, thread to ledger), `ledger.mjs` (optional `observe` block, `null` when absent — tolerated by `ledger-reader.mjs`).\n17\t- **Given-When-Then:** small output → tier `none`, BYPASS no model call; big+complex → frontier escalate (genuine `tokens>frontier && complex` conjunction — size alone never escalates), raw recoverable byte-for-byte via existing `read-raw.mjs`, `tokens_saved − observe_cost` recorded and >0 on escalate.\n18\t- **Review:** 2 independent refuters both flagged the SAME defect (agreement) — an orphan dead-code `observe.mjs` (unimported/untested/divergent) the EXECUTE agent shipped alongside the wired module. **FIX:** deleted the orphan (untracked, zero importers). Re-gate GREEN, no new findings.\n19\t- **Gate (orchestrator-run):** **174 pass / 0 fail** (was 161; +13). Converged in 1 fix-iter.\n20\t\n21\t### Wave 3 — E3 Tier routers (renamed from \"MoE\") — ✅ GREEN\n22\t\n23\t- **Built:** `gwl-t2r-brain/harness/tier-routers.mjs` (`pretasteRouter` predictive-only; `reasoningRouter` verify-then-escalate cascade with terminal frontier stop; `summaryRouter` wrapping Wave-2 `observeGate`; `detectOOD` heuristic, `DEFAULT_VERIFY_THRESHOLDS` — cheapest tier strictest bar per constraint 5) + `tier-routers.test.mjs` (17 tests: 3 per-router eval blocks + 3 GWT). Reuses existing `routing-matrix.mjs` tier vocabulary; no fork. No existing source modified.\n24\t- **Given-When-Then:** easy → cheap tier chosen + output verified; cheap output fails verify → escalates one tier up (cascade to frontier); OOD input → frontier with no cheap burn. Verifier gates on the produced OUTPUT's confidence (not taste). Naming: \"tier router\" throughout, no reviewer-facing \"MoE\".\n25\t- **Review:** 2 independent refuters both GO; the two candidate-MAJORs (clone router / misplaced verifier) refuted. **FIX:** applied W3-F1 (LOW, but a latent constraint-2 violation) — OOD now wins over an explicit `startTier` override so an OOD turn always fails up to frontier. Pre-existing `selectTier` MINOR quirks left out of scope.\n26\t- **Gate (orchestrator-run):** **191 pass / 0 fail** (was 174; +17). Converged in 1 fix-iter.\n27\t\n28\t### Wave 4 — E4 Memory (two-track session + Store C knowledge) — ✅ GREEN\n29\t\n30\t- **Built:** `gwl-t2r-brain/harness/memory.mjs` (Store A running-summary, Store B raw-turn append/retrieve, Store C `KnowledgeStoreC` — cosine-indexed shards reusing the exact D3 Shard schema, injectable 384-d embedder, file-based JSONL, manual seed/append; `recordTurn` turn-complete hook; `pretasteLocalContext` cosine top-k retrieval) + `memory.test.mjs` (18 tests, offline, `os.tmpdir()` only). Additive — no existing source modified.\n31\t- **Given-When-Then:** turn completes → A updated + B persisted/retrievable; sharpened query → pre-taste (ii) returns top-k Store-C shards by cosine (proven to read Store C and NOT the lossy summary via a mango-summary/docker-shard separation test); rank order + confidence-scaling + cross-session reload verified.\n32\t- **Review:** 2 independent refuters both GO. The key question — done-when \"updates each turn\" with `recordTurn` as a helper not yet wired into the live loop — was decisively ruled NOT a gap (plan Deliverables = stores + retrieval path; live prompt-assembly wiring is Wave 5 / D2). Schema-reuse-vs-reinvent judged defensible (D3 record canonical; in-code shard modules diverge). MINORs only (cosine-index filename cosmetic; read-path access-tracking write) — non-blocking, no agreement.\n33\t- **Gate (orchestrator-run):** **209 pass / 0 fail** (was 191; +18). Converged in 0 fix-iters.\n34\t\n35\t### Wave 5 — E5 Caching discipline — ✅ GREEN\n36\t\n37\t- **Built:** `gwl-t2r-brain/harness/caching.mjs` (`renderUncachedTail` folding Store-A summary + Store-C knowledge + sharpened input into the volatile tail; `stablePrefixHash`/`refreshTail` proving a summary rewrite leaves the cached prefix anchor byte-stable; `PerTierPrefix` append-only per-tier instruction/skill anchor; `CacheReadByTier` → ledger block) + `e5-caching.test.mjs` (11 tests). Additive `ledger.mjs` edit: optional `cache_read_by_tier` row field, `null` when absent (mirrors Wave-2 `observe`). `prompt.mjs` untouched.\n38\t- **Given-When-Then:** summary update rewrites the TAIL but the cached PREFIX hash is unchanged AND `cache_read > 0` (proof discriminates: stable prefix → positive, busted prefix → 0); per-tier `cache_read` recorded in the ledger and read back.\n39\t- **Review:** Reviewer #1 GO (verified the prefix-stability proof is non-vacuous). Reviewer #2 raised one MAJOR (F2-1) + two MINOR. **Adjudication:** F2-1 (Part-3 LOCAL-rolling-truncation / FRONTIER-hard-turn-gating not implemented) is single-reviewer (below the 2-agree BLOCKER bar) AND superseded — **D2 reconciles Part-3's per-tier verbatim transcript away**, making the per-tier cumulative the stable instruction/skill *anchor* (which append-only correctly delivers). **FIX** applied for the fair honesty sub-points: F2-2 — added a real `MIN_CACHEABLE_TOKENS=1024` floor to the cache simulator + sized the fixture prefix above it + a load-bearing sub-floor test (E5-4b) so `cache_read>0` is a real floor-clearing win; F2-3 — softened the `caching.mjs` header that overstated \"WIRES\" to reflect it's the tail-composer seam the loop will call.\n40\t- **Gate (orchestrator-run):** **220 pass / 0 fail** (was 209; +11). Converged in 1 fix-iter.\n41\t\n42\t### Wave 6 — E6 Training-data capture — ✅ GREEN\n43\t\n44\t- **Built:** `gwl-t2r-brain/harness/training-capture.mjs` (`TrainingCapture` append-JSONL capture of `(raw_input, output, chosen_tier, outcome)` per routed turn; `captureFromRouter` reads `chosen_tier` off a Wave-3 router result; `mulberry32` seeded PRNG + `sampleSubset` reproducible partial Fisher-Yates — no `Math.random()`/`Date.now()`; `microSleep` Tier-1 $0 session-close consolidation: dedup + promote-to-Store-C via the existing `KnowledgeStoreC.seed()` path, no LLM/network) + `training-capture.test.mjs` (22 tests). Capture-only — no training/distill/LoRA. Additive, no existing source modified.\n45\t- **Given-When-Then:** routed turn → labeled JSONL record appended; session close → micro-sleep consolidates with NO model-training call (throwing-model witness proves zero model reach). Same-seed → byte-identical sample (proven independent of global RNG perturbation).\n46\t- **Review:** 2 independent refuters, no BLOCKER (highest-value attack — input→tier linkage for trainability — came back clean). **FIX** applied for three real-but-non-blocking defects: R1-F1 — 3 stray NUL bytes made the source register as *binary* (violated repo encoding discipline) → replaced separator, file now clean UTF-8; R2-F1 — `microSleep` re-promoted into Store C every run (3→6→9) → now idempotent (promoted-marker persisted, skipped on re-run) + new \"twice ⇒ size unchanged\" test; R2-F2 — numeric vs string seed divergence → canonicalized so `42 === \"42\"` + test.\n47\t- **Gate (orchestrator-run):** **242 pass / 0 fail** (was 220; +22). Converged in 1 fix-iter.\n48\t\n49\t### Wave 7 — E7 A/B evaluation (three-way) — ✅ GREEN\n50\t\n51\t- **Built:** `gwl-t2r-brain/harness/eval-ab.mjs` (pinned-harness config + fingerprint assert gate; `makeT2RBrain` — the t2r arm ASSEMBLED from prior waves: `pickLock`←Wave-3 `pretasteRouter`, `compress`←Wave-2 `observeGate`, `reason`←production clients; `runMultiArmEval` multi-run runner + privacy probe; `dominates`/`paretoFrontier`/`buildParetoReport`; `makeThreeWayArms` — Opus-4.8 baseline · t2r · Sovereign) + `eval-ab.test.mjs` (21 tests). Offline/deterministic (injected fake transports per arm); proves the MECHANISM, not live benchmark numbers. Additive — no existing source modified.\n52\t- **Given-When-Then:** pinned harness + task set → each of the 3 brains run n≥2× → per-brain cost (real ledger) + quality + privacy on a Pareto frontier; the Sovereign arm's report flags **zero third-party calls** (probe distinguishes `api.anthropic.com`/`googleapis.com` from `127.0.0.1`/`localhost`, spoof-resistant). All three arms `isBrain`-conform and drive the SAME pinned `runLoopWithBrain`.\n53\t- **Review:** Reviewer #1 fully clean GO (verified the t2r arm is a genuine Wave 2–6 composition, not a renamed Opus; Pareto dominance correct; privacy axis load-bearing). Reviewer #2 GO with 3 single-reviewer findings → **FIX** applied: F1 (MAJOR-observational) — added a decisive-accuracy test proving the quality axis changes the Pareto outcome (would fail if quality were dropped), so all three axes are now provably load-bearing; F2 (MINOR) — deepened the pinned-harness fingerprint to cover tool description + inputSchema (catches drift it claimed to); F3 (MINOR) — surfaced a per-arm abort/failure tally independent of the scorer.\n54\t- **Gate (orchestrator-run):** **263 pass / 0 fail** (was 242; +21). Converged in 1 fix-iter.\n55\t\n56\t---\n57\t\n58\t## PROJECT DONE — Phase E (GWL t2r Brain) ✅\n59\t\n60\tAll 7 waves GREEN via the orchestrator-run gate. Final gate: **`node --test gwl-t2r-brain/harness/*.test.mjs` → 263 pass / 0 fail** (started from the 154-test harness-GA baseline; +109 across the seven waves). North Star met: the efficient **t2r brain is built and three-way A/B-measured** (cost-accuracy-privacy Pareto, multi-run) against the **Opus-4.8 baseline** and a **fully-local/sovereign** brain on the one pinned, brain-agnostic harness. Build constraints honored throughout: **tier routers** (not \"MoE\"), verifier on the reasoning tier, summary + knowledge in the **uncached tail**, **`read_raw`** recoverability, **each router its own eval**, **heuristic-first → distill-later** (capture-now). Sequenced Phase-F (sleep-training / organism / Lorentz) remains deliberately out of scope.\n61\t\n62\tCommits: Wave 1 `db3efc34` · Wave 2 `ed2f9faa` · Wave 3 `c1db114e` · Wave 4 `3ca050c6` · Wave 5 `c5b955d9` · Wave 6 `293f1320` · Wave 7 `eedaff75`.\n63\t\n64\t### Follow-on (post-Phase-E) — live-eval driver\n65\t\n66\t- **Built** `gwl-t2r-brain/harness/live-eval.mjs` + `live-eval.test.mjs` (11 offline tests) — a runner that drives the Wave-7 eval machinery against **real** transports to emit real cost-accuracy-privacy numbers. Real fs tool executor (`list_directory`/`read_file`, path-contained), a 3-task rubric-scored task set (real accuracy axis), `preflightLive` (ANTHROPIC_API_KEY + ollama reachable + model pulled; never spends on failure), and `--synthetic` (offline, gated) vs `--live` (real, operator-run) modes. Additive `eval-ab.mjs` edit: `makeThreeWayArms` threads an optional `localModel` (defaults unchanged). **Run:** `node gwl-t2r-brain/harness/live-eval.mjs --live --runs 3` (needs the key + ollama + a ~7–8B model pulled on gwl-server). Reviewed clean (no accidental-spend path; containment sound). Gate **274/274**.\n67\t\n68\t- **LIVE RUN on gwl-server (2026-06-11) — two real harness bugs found + fixed via the Foreman adversarial loop, then a clean three-way result:**\n69\t  - **Bug 1 — parser strictness** (`step.mjs:260`): only accepted `action:\"tool_call\"`; local/gemini models emit `action:\"<toolname>\"` → their tool calls were dropped → no-progress aborts. **Fix** (commit `9c3bb3f2`, 2 reviewers GO): additive rescue — `action:\"<knownTool>\"` (gated on `ctx.toolNames`) normalizes to a tool_call; rescued calls re-enter the full guard chain; production `tool_call`/`final_answer` byte-identical.\n70\t  - **Bug 2 — fs-tool signature mismatch** (`live-eval.mjs`): `makeFsRunTool` used `runTool(call)` but the loop calls `runTool(name, params, ctx)` positionally (`step.mjs:409`) → every call returned `unknown tool \"undefined\"` → no model got file data → all arms scored ~0 (the *real* cause, not 7B capability). **Fix** (commit `263d7e5c`, 2 reviewers GO): canonical positional signature + an end-to-end test that fails under the old signature. Free local verify: qwen 3/3 correct.\n71\t  - **Security:** the report had leaked the Gemini `?key=` into `logs/` (gitignored, scrubbed); `redactUrl` now strips secrets from recorded URLs (commit `62098cc3`).\n72\t  - **Definitive result** (gate **288/288**; `--live --runs 3`): **opus-4-7 $0.0268 q1.00 (18 third-party)** · **gemini-3.5-flash $0.0090 q1.00 (21 third-party)** · **sovereign qwen2.5:7b $0.0000 q1.00 (0 third-party, ★ sole Pareto-optimal)**. On these simple fs tasks all three tie at quality 1.0, so the local arm dominates on cost+privacy. **Caveat:** simple tasks — harder synthesis would separate quality (D6); grow the task set next. Total spend ~$0.10.\n73\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01R7onNqhV8BYzhXq32rMA1B","session_id":"75eda862-34e1-4a42-a5f6-73eb4ef1cd9a","uuid":"f6c0d22a-ad43-4358-a3b1-9d2d2ee0928d","timestamp":"2026-06-23T18:18:15.163Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Ground Gandalf diagnosis of Agentic-Home"}
