{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0172NFa5dUD3Lt2Jd1ahUk9a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# GWL t2r Brain — Implementation Plan (Foreman-ready)\n2\t\n3\ttest-command: node --test gwl-t2r-brain/harness/*.test.mjs\n4\t\n5\t**North Star:** The efficient t2r brain is built and proven by A/B measurement against the Opus-4.8 baseline AND a fully-local/sovereign brain on the same pinned harness — a three-way cost-accuracy-privacy comparison.\n6\t\n7\t## Success criteria\n8\t- (7) The t2r brain (per the DESIGN doc) is built and A/B-measured vs the Opus-4.8 baseline and a fully-local/sovereign brain on the pinned harness (cost-accuracy-privacy Pareto, multi-run).\n9\t- Build constraints: tier routers (not \"MoE\"); verifier on the reasoning tier; summary+knowledge in the uncached tail; `read_raw` recoverability; each router its own eval; heuristic-first → distill-later.\n10\t\n11\t> SEQUENCED — do NOT start this handoff until Criteria 1–6 (the `t2r-harness-to-GA` handoff) are met. **As of 2026-06-10 the harness handoff is GA (8/8 GREEN), so this handoff is UNBLOCKED.** Every wave ships real source its new tests import and exercise; acceptance criteria follow the D16 hybrid convention. Full architecture + decisions D1–D6: `docs/plans/DESIGN-t2r-brain-and-gwl-harness-2026-06-08.md`.\n12\t>\n13\t> **t2rs reconcile (Part 6 / D7–D9, locked 2026-06-09):** this handoff is the **v0 layer of the t2rs ladder** — Part 6 confirms \"at v0 (Phase E) each stage is a single lean model + flat Store-C; the Phase-F track grows each stage toward the full ~11-cell organism,\" so the waves below are consistent and need no re-architecture. **Naming:** this handoff intentionally keeps the **\"t2r\"** vocabulary (D7) to avoid disrupting the build; the Taste→Reason→**Summary** rename + the three-organism evolution live in the DESIGN doc Part 6 and the Phase-F handoffs (`plans/foreman/F-A-t2rs-sleep`, `F-B-t2rs-lorentz-memory`, `F-C-t2rs-organism`), which are SEQUENCED after this one. Read Part 6 (D7–D9) alongside D1–D6 before building.\n14\t\n15\t## Wave 1 — E1 Brain-seam contract (+ baseline & sovereign controls)\n16\t\n17\t**Intent:** Formalize the pluggable brain interface so any brain drives the same harness; ship the Opus-4.8 baseline brain and a fully-local/sovereign OSS brain as measured controls.\n18\t\n19\t**Deliverables:** a documented brain interface (`pickLock`/`reason`/`compress`); the Opus-4.8 baseline brain adapter; a fully-local/sovereign OSS brain adapter (~7–8B on the 4070); a conformance test any brain must pass. **The seam is model-size-agnostic (D9):** swapping a bigger model into any stage (7–8B → 70B-class → 671B-class as hardware allows) is a CONFIG change, not a re-architecture.\n20\t\n21\t**Depends on:** —\n22\t\n23\t**done-when:** the Opus-4.8 baseline brain and the local-OSS brain both satisfy the conformance test driving the harness loop, with the local brain making zero third-party calls; the seam accepts a different model id per stage with no interface change (D9).\n24\t\n25\t- **Given** the brain-seam conformance suite, **when** the Opus-4.8 brain is plugged in, **then** a harness loop completes.\n26\t- **Given** the conformance suite, **when** the fully-local OSS brain is plugged in, **then** the same loop completes with no third-party network call.\n27\t- **Given** the size-agnostic seam (D9), **when** a stage's model id is swapped via config, **then** the conformance suite still passes with no interface/code change.\n28\t\n29\t## Wave 2 — E2 Observe gated context-worker\n30\t\n31\t**Intent:** Build step-6 as a gated compression worker with raw fallback and a net-savings meter (not a co-equal brain). **This worker is the t2rs \"Summary\" stage at v0 (D7/D8)** — a single lean summarizer now; Phase F-C grows it into the third ~11-cell organism. (The harness already ships the `compress` seam + an F6 compressor that this wave formalizes into the gated none/local/frontier worker.)\n32\t\n33\t**Deliverables:** a pre-Observe gate (none/local/frontier); local + frontier summarizers; `read_raw` recoverability; a per-turn net-savings (`tokens_saved − observe_cost`) meter.\n34\t\n35\t**Depends on:** E1 Brain-seam contract\n36\t\n37\t**done-when:** small outputs bypass, normal outputs get a local summary, big+complex escalate; the raw observation is always recoverable; the meter records net savings per turn.\n38\t\n39\t- **Given** a small tool output, **when** Observe runs, **then** it bypasses with no model call.\n40\t- **Given** a large complex output, **when** Observe runs, **then** it escalates and the raw remains addressable via `read_raw`, and `tokens_saved − observe_cost` is recorded.\n41\t\n42\t## Wave 3 — E3 Tier routers (renamed from \"MoE\")\n43\t\n44\t**Intent:** Build the three difficulty routers (taste / reasoning / summary) with a verifier on the reasoning tier and heuristic-first defaults.\n45\t\n46\t**Deliverables:** pre-taste, reasoning, and summary tier routers; a verify-then-escalate fallback on the reasoning tier; OOD-fails-up-to-frontier; heuristic/prompted defaults (no training yet).\n47\t\n48\t**Depends on:** E2 Observe gated context-worker\n49\t\n50\t**done-when:** each router selects a tier from the input; the reasoning router verifies the cheap output and escalates on low confidence; an OOD input routes up to frontier; tests green.\n51\t\n52\t- **Given** an easy input, **when** the reasoning router runs, **then** a cheap tier is chosen and its output verified.\n53\t- **Given** the cheap output fails verification, **when** the router re-evaluates, **then** it escalates to a higher tier.\n54\t- **Given** an out-of-distribution input, **when** routed, **then** it goes to the frontier tier.\n55\t\n56\t## Wave 4 — E4 Memory (two-track session + Store C knowledge)\n57\t\n58\t**Intent:** Two-track session memory (running summary + raw store) plus the Store C knowledge shards (Knowledge-Linear) feeding pre-taste (ii).\n59\t\n60\t**Deliverables:** a running-summary store (A); a raw-turn store (B); Store C — a cosine-indexed Shard store reusing the existing Shard schema; pre-taste (ii) retrieval from Store C.\n61\t\n62\t**Depends on:** E3 Tier routers\n63\t\n64\t**done-when:** the running summary updates each turn; raw turns are retrievable; pre-taste (ii) retrieves top-k knowledge shards by cosine from Store C; retrieval test green.\n65\t\n66\t- **Given** a session, **when** a turn completes, **then** the running summary is updated and the raw turn persisted.\n67\t- **Given** a sharpened query, **when** pre-taste (ii) runs, **then** it attaches top-k Store-C shards as local context, retrieved from the knowledge/raw stores — not the lossy summary.\n68\t\n69\t## Wave 5 — E5 Caching discipline\n70\t\n71\t**Intent:** Keep the mutable summary + selected knowledge in the uncached tail; anchor caching on the stable skill/instruction prefix; measure `cache_read` per tier.\n72\t\n73\t**Deliverables:** a tail/prefix split for the brain prompts; a per-tier cumulative prefix; a `cache_read`-per-tier ledger assertion.\n74\t\n75\t**Depends on:** E4 Memory (two-track session + Store C knowledge)\n76\t\n77\t**done-when:** updating the summary each turn does not bust the cached prefix; `cache_read` > 0 on the stable prefix; per-tier `cache_read` is recorded; test green.\n78\t\n79\t- **Given** a turn that updates the running summary, **when** the prompt is built, **then** the cached skill/instruction prefix hash is unchanged and `cache_read` > 0.\n80\t- **Given** each tier, **when** it runs, **then** its `cache_read` is recorded in the ledger.\n81\t\n82\t## Wave 6 — E6 Training-data capture\n83\t\n84\t**Intent:** Capture router training data (input → sharpened/summarized output, chosen tier) for later sleep-training. Capture now, train later.\n85\t\n86\t**Deliverables:** a capture path writing (raw input, output, chosen-tier, outcome) records; reproducible random-subset sampling; a Tier-1 micro-sleep hook (no model-training call yet).\n87\t\n88\t**Depends on:** E5 Caching discipline\n89\t\n90\t**done-when:** each routed turn appends a labeled training record; sampling is reproducible; capture has tests.\n91\t\n92\t- **Given** a routed turn, **when** it completes, **then** a training record (raw input, sharpened/summarized output, chosen tier) is appended.\n93\t- **Given** a session close, **when** micro-sleep runs, **then** records are consolidated with no model-training call.\n94\t\n95\t## Wave 7 — E7 A/B evaluation (three-way)\n96\t\n97\t**Intent:** Measure the brains against each other on the pinned harness — Opus-4.8 baseline vs t2r vs fully-local/sovereign — on a cost-accuracy-privacy Pareto, multi-run.\n98\t\n99\t**Deliverables:** an A/B eval harness pinning tools+prompts+version; a multi-run runner over a task set; a cost-accuracy-privacy Pareto report including the fully-local arm.\n100\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01R7onNqhV8BYzhXq32rMA1B","session_id":"75eda862-34e1-4a42-a5f6-73eb4ef1cd9a","uuid":"7cf49968-9aa2-4be0-bad2-d2cf1eb456ea","timestamp":"2026-06-23T18:18:20.460Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Ground Gandalf diagnosis of Agentic-Home"}
