{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HZ8cvtwZdsnuLJcs9Uz29U","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# CLAUDE.md — Workspace Root\n2\t\n3\tThis file orients any Claude Code (or other coding-agent) session opened at the workspace root. Read it first.\n4\t\n5\t## Canonical workspace location (updated 2026-05-12)\n6\t\n7\t**The canonical workspace is `C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home\\` on the `gwl-server` box** — Dell XPS 8960, Windows hostname `PUTER`, Tailscale identity `gwl-server.tailb49f65.ts.net` / `100.69.215.4`. Specs: Intel Core i9-13900K (24c/32t), 32 GB DDR5-4800 (single-DIMM, single-channel — punch-list upgrade is a matched second stick), **NVIDIA RTX 4070 12 GB VRAM** (CUDA 13.0, compute cap 8.9, Ada), C: 1.8 TB OS NVMe + D: 1.9 TB empty NVMe earmarked for the training corpus + LoRA checkpoints + model weights + E: 1.7 TB external Samsung exFAT. High Performance power plan, 1 Gbps wired, Hyper-V enabled. Full survey: `logs\\gwl-server-survey-2026-05-12-114818.txt`; rerun any time via `scripts\\Survey-GWL-Server.ps1`.\n8\t\n9\tThe workspace lives on local NVMe — *not* in OneDrive. The previous OneDrive copy at `C:\\Users\\jcl12\\OneDrive - Axmra\\NextGen\\Agentic Home\\` is retained as a passive backup only; do not edit it, and do not point scripts/configs at it. OneDrive's file-on-demand sync engine was causing webpack cache corruption (`UNKNOWN errno -4094`), `routing.json` write races between machines, and `~/.openclaw` session-lock contention that stretched single agent turns to 5+ minutes. Initial off-OneDrive migration ran 2026-05-01 via `scripts/migrate-to-local.ps1`. The **laptop → gwl-server host move** happened on 2026-05-12 — the laptop (`s1-jliechty-pl`, still on Tailscale) is now a development client, not the canonical host. **All future work happens here on gwl-server in `C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home`.**\n10\t\n11\t**Why the host move matters for Phase C.** The laptop had no usable training GPU. The gwl-server's RTX 4070 (12 GB VRAM, Ada) unblocks Phase C of Wave 7 — specifically the G-32 LoRA activation against the adjudicator-training-tuple corpus we've been accumulating since 2026-05-08, plus the G-28 skill-evolution enable. The 12 GB VRAM bounds us to **QLoRA fine-tuning on ≤8B student models** (Llama-3.1-8B / Qwen-2.5-7B class, 4-bit quantized via `unsloth` or `bitsandbytes`); full-precision training and 13B+ models stay off-card. That's by design — the brain architecture is \"distill from frontier into small local students.\"\n12\t\n13\t**Master skill repo is now also local** at `C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home\\skills-master\\` (moved out of the PSU OneDrive on 2026-05-07 evening). Same reasoning: OneDrive's Files-On-Demand was causing `[System.IO.File]::ReadAllBytes` \"cloud operation is invalid\" errors during `Bootstrap-Agentic-Home.ps1`. The legacy PSU OneDrive path (`C:\\Users\\jcl12\\OneDrive - The Pennsylvania State University\\Research\\AI Skill Repo\\Agent Review\\skills\\`) is retained as a read-only fallback in the bootstrap + agent-chat resolvers for cross-machine compatibility, but **all writes go to the local copy**. Cross-machine availability and durable backup will eventually move to a server + cloud-backup story (Backblaze B2 / Cloudflare R2 / GitHub remote per `project-manager-kit/references/backup-options.md`); that's a deliberate future migration, not a today action.\n14\t\n15\t## Versioning (canonical — see `VERSIONING.md`)\n16\t\n17\tGWL **system version = `v<BRAIN>.<HARNESS>`**. BRAIN = t2r brain generation; HARNESS = agentic harness/capacity (OpenClaw + G-Brain + Helping Hand/Aurora). **Current: `v2.1`** — gen-2 dynamic-context t2r brain (live) + gen-1 harness. Build iterations within a generation are tracked by date+commit, not a version digit (the old \"v2.2/v2.3/v2.5\" labels were gen-2 brain builds, not system bumps). Distinct from the **v0–v1–v2 agent-rollout ladder** (agent maturity stage): `alpha-v0` is a v0-ladder agent **vehicle** running the `v2.1` system — agent id ≠ system version.\n18\t\n19\t## What this workspace is\n20\t\n21\tJohn Liechty's **Agentic Sandbox** — a research workspace for building, training, and evaluating clusters of AI agents. The active deliverable is the **Ghost World Labs (GWL-M)** master GUI, a Next.js app (`sandbox-lab-gui/`) that launches and supervises agents running on the **OpenClaw** runtime (MIT-licensed, installed globally via npm).\n22\t\n23\tThe sandbox is a research project, not a production system. Most folders at the root contain design documents (whitepapers, plans, session logs); a smaller number contain runnable code.\n24\t\n25\t## Read this before doing anything\n26\t\n27\t- **There is a subfolder-scoped CLAUDE.md** at `Sandbox Setup Package/CLAUDE.md` covering the Lite/Full deployment workflow. It applies only to that folder.\n28\t- **Recent session handoffs** at the root: the most recent first. `SESSION-HANDOFF-Alpha-Recovery-2026-04-29-PM.md` was the last paused execution; everything in it has now landed.\n29\t- **The two plan documents at the root** — `PLAN-Alpha-GUI-Recovery.md` and `PLAN-Code-Improvements-Round-2.md` — are the source of truth for the recovery + improvements work executed up to commit `916c6bf`.\n30\t- **John is non-technical.** Pair concepts with concrete commands. Don't lecture. Names occasionally get misheard — OpenClaw, Peter Steinberger, Gary Tan's GBrain, Andrej Karpathy — correct in passing.\n31\t\n32\t## The Ghost World Labs GUI — how it actually runs\n33\t\n34\tEntry point: `Launch-Ghost-World-Labs.bat` at the workspace root.\n35\t\n36\tFlow:\n37\t\n38\t1. The `.bat` cleans up any process listening on port 3001, then `cd`s into `sandbox-lab-gui/` and runs `npm run dev`.\n39\t2. `npm run dev` runs `node server.mjs`, a custom Next.js + WebSocket server.\n40\t3. `server.mjs` reads `../.env` (the workspace-root `.env`) to inherit `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` and `GEMINI_API_KEY`. **It re-reads `.env` on every PTY spawn, so a key saved through the Settings Vault takes effect on the next terminal launch — no server restart needed.**\n41\t4. The browser opens to `http://localhost:3001`. The dashboard pre-creates three terminals: `gemini` (Gemini CLI), `claude` (Claude Code), and `alpha` (the Alpha Agent via `node agent-chat.mjs alpha`).\n42\t5. Clicking another agent tile in the right-hand Agent Matrix spawns a new terminal running `node agent-chat.mjs <id>`.\n43\t6. `agent-chat.mjs` reads the per-agent provider/model from `Sandbox Setup Package/config/routing.json` (the canonical file), validates that the matching API key is present, and spawns `openclaw agent --agent <id> --local --verbose on -m <message>`. If the key is missing, it fails fast with a clear message pointing to the Settings Vault.\n44\t\n45\tThe server auto-shuts-down 10s after the last GUI window closes.\n46\t\n47\t## The API-key contract\n48\t\n49\t| Surface | What it uses |\n50\t|---|---|\n51\t| The user's own Claude Code / Cowork session (this file's reader) | Anthropic Cowork **subscription** — no API key. |\n52\t| The \"Claude Code\" terminal inside the GWL GUI | The user's Cowork subscription via `claude login`. |\n53\t| The \"Gemini CLI\" terminal inside the GWL GUI | Gemini Code Assist / free tier (no API key needed). |\n54\t| **The Alpha Agent and every other agent launched from the GUI** | **API keys** — `GEMINI_API_KEY` for Google providers, `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` for Anthropic providers. Stored in the workspace `.env`, edited via the Settings Vault. |\n55\t\n56\tThe boundary is intentional. Agents inside the sandbox spend metered API budget; the user's interactive coding session does not. **Do not confuse the two.** Do not make API calls from a Claude Code / Cowork session that would draw on the user's Anthropic API key.\n57\t\n58\t## The agent registry\n59\t\n60\tCanonical routing: `Sandbox Setup Package/config/routing.json`. Keys at the top level: `defaults`, `global_flags`, `by_agent`. The Settings Vault GET/POST writes here. The Vault and the agent-chat launcher are the only readers.\n61\t\n62\tCurrently built and operational. **Default AgentMatrix view shows only the v0 daily-use vehicle** (alpha-v0) per commit `99c6ccbf`; everything else lives behind the \"Show research & legacy agents\" toggle.\n63\t\n64\t**v0 daily-use vehicle** (the agent John actually reaches for through the GUI tile):\n65\t\n66\t- `alpha-v0` — Daily-use general-purpose t2r agent. Routes through `sandbox-lab-gui/agent-chat-v0.mjs` (PTY wrapper) which imports `dispatchTurn` from `sandbox-lab-gui/brain/dispatcher/t2r-dispatcher.mjs`. Both halves Gemini 3.1 Pro by default (`taste_model` + `reasoning_model` in `routing.json` `by_agent.alpha-v0`). $100/month wallet enforced at dispatcher. 7-skill bundle: `deep-think`, `deep-research`, `expert-coder`, `expert-coder-Win11`, `project-manager`, `family-accountant`, `use-claude-code`. Persona at `Sandbox Setup Package/PERSONAS/global/alpha-v0-personal-manager.md`. Project picker reads `Sandbox Setup Package/config/projects.json` (9 seeds as of 2026-05-16). Per-project transcripts at `<project-cwd>/.alpha/transcript.jsonl`. Multi-window per project (\"each project a different window\" like Cowork) per `PLAN-Alpha-GUI-Integration-2026-05-15.md` §B6. Shipped commits `6250cf5a` + `6482d06d` 2026-05-15/16. **v0 specialists** (sibling agents to alpha-v0, same dispatcher, different skill bundle + persona prompt + default project binding) land Sprint S2 — `finance-alpha` + `code-alpha` per `PLAN-Master-Plan-Update-Specialists-2026-05-16.md` §B.\n67\t\n68\t**Research & legacy agents** (hidden by default in AgentMatrix; toggle to reveal):\n69\t\n70\t- `alpha` — Legacy tile, routes to brain-research v2 orchestrator (`brain/orchestrator.mjs` via `agent-chat.mjs` L818 `startsWith('alpha')` bypass). NOT the v0 daily-use path — that's alpha-v0. Persona at `alpha-personal-manager.md`. Kept side-by-side with alpha-v0 during S1/S2; tile-collapse decision deferred to S2 per `PLAN-Alpha-GUI-Integration-2026-05-15.md` §3.A1.\n71\t- `sigma` — Memory schema research. Anthropic (`claude-sonnet-4-6`).\n72\t- `prime-coder` — Codes the GUI and harness scripts. Anthropic (`claude-opus-4-7`), 16k token budget.\n73\t- `alpha-linear` / `alpha-lorentz` — SOUL-twin brain-research pilots (linear / Lorentz-hyperbolic bases). Not part of v0 daily use; alive for Phase B GLCI work.\n74\t\n75\tEverything else in `routing.json` (`dean`, `lambda`, `phi`, `ccr`, `w-*`, `s-*`) is planned but not yet built. The `AgentMatrix.tsx` component grays them out and offers to spawn an Interactive Builder when clicked.\n76\t\n77\t**Model id source-of-truth:** `sandbox-lab-gui/app/lib/models.ts` (`KNOWN_MODELS`). The Settings Vault dropdowns and `agent-chat.mjs`'s `/model` validation both read from this. When adding a new model id, update this file (and the small `AGENT_KNOWN_MODELS` mirror inside `agent-chat.mjs` for the slash-command path). The `verified` flag flips to `true` only after a real OpenClaw turn returns a successful response with that id.\n78\t\n79\t**Per-turn routing:** `agent-chat.mjs` re-reads `routing.json` at the start of every Enter, so a model change saved in the Settings Vault (or via `/model <id>`) takes effect on the next turn without closing the terminal.\n80\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01R7onNqhV8BYzhXq32rMA1B","session_id":"75eda862-34e1-4a42-a5f6-73eb4ef1cd9a","uuid":"f302c075-cb62-4b8a-894a-932e2f534115","timestamp":"2026-06-23T18:18:27.931Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Ground Gandalf diagnosis of Agentic-Home"}
