{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K2K2Eg9eVc9vpPUB5gvb5m","type":"tool_result","content":"C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home/docs/plans/PLAN-Sovereign-T2R-Harness-Implementation-v2.md:**Through-line (Architect):** cache-stability — correctly discovered — silently demotes three marquee gold-standard features (per-step tiering, per-step skill selection, per-step local savings) from \"per-step\" to \"loop-scoped or unvalidated.\" The architecture is sound; the *claims* weren't honest about what cache-stability costs. v2 fixes the claims, the two P0 bugs, and gates the spend.\nC:\\dev\\Agentic-Home/docs/plans/PLAN-Sovereign-T2R-Harness-Implementation-v2.md:A rigorous flaw-hunt on the gold standard and the plan found the architecture sound but the *case* over-claimed: the headline −56% rests on an unvalidated local-model competence bet (prior art ⇒ realistic ~−30–35%, much of it capturable by extending OpenClaw), \"tier every step\" is really loop-locked, and there are two P0 correctness bugs (lossy one-way compression; a broken no-progress metric). v2 **gates the entire build behind a 1-day spike** with a three-way go/no-go (raw gateway / extend-OpenClaw-compression / harness) — build the harness only if local sub-decisions clear ~85% success and beat the *extend* baseline by a margin worth the rebuild; otherwise ship the compression inside an OpenClaw plugin. It also fixes the P0/P1 defects: a `read_raw` affordance + extractive compression, a plan-state progress counter, a tail budget, a normalized hash + `resetCache`, and side-effect idempotency. Everything else (two layers, cache discipline, bounded loop, POD-debug-state, reuse, feature-flag cutover) carries forward. **Recommended next action: run the Phase-0 spike — it decides whether to build at all.**","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01R7onNqhV8BYzhXq32rMA1B","session_id":"75eda862-34e1-4a42-a5f6-73eb4ef1cd9a","uuid":"8fccb201-adc9-4e6f-b5c4-084cc65bfb91","timestamp":"20