{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CWhAPTMivLLmeipiYzFPGd","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# INDEPENDENT VALIDATION REPORT — Sovereign t2r Harness\n2\t\n3\t## 0. RESOLUTION (2026-05-29, post-review)\n4\tBoth P0 defects were **independently reproduced** (own repros, not just the reviewer's word) and **FIXED**:\n5\t- **P0-1** — `clients.mjs` now uses the accumulated streamed TEXT as the commit signal (`estOut = output || approxTokens(text)`) at both failure sites, driving BOTH the retry decision (mid-stream sever after streamed text ⇒ fatal, not retried — no double-bill) and the ledger (books the estimated cost, not $0). New **real-parser** regression test `P0 mid-stream:` (no mock) — it fails on the old code.\n6\t- **P0-2** — `server.mjs` `resolveHarnessCommand` now hard-protects `alpha-v0` (`PROTECTED_GATEWAY_AGENTS`) — it can never route to the harness even if listed. New regression test `P0 gateway-protection:` loads the real `server.mjs` source.\n7\t- **Test-mocking gap** (the reviewer's fair critique) closed: the new mid-stream test exercises the real `reasonAnthropic` stream parser, not a mock.\n8\tTests: harness 41→43 green; brain 61; live gate PASS. The reviewer's calibration note: \"unbounded\" double-billing is actually bounded to the retry cap (≤3×) — still a real cost/ledger bug, now fixed. Committed in `7208d085`.\n9\t\n10\t**Re-check (the fix-of-a-fix discipline, 2026-05-29):** two right-sized adversarial agents re-verified the P0 fixes against the real code. **P0-1 PASS** (verified against reconstructed pre-fix code; the test fails on old code; no regression). **P0-2 INCOMPLETE → strengthened:** the first fix only guarded the `-gateway.mjs` input form, but `query.cmd` is client-controlled + unauthenticated and `resolveAlphaV0Command` accepts `-harness`, so a crafted `node agent-chat-v0-harness.mjs alpha-v0` bypassed it. Final fix makes `resolveHarnessCommand` **server-control** the script (normalize to gateway, promote to harness ONLY for a flag-listed non-protected agent) — the client can no longer influence the harness-vs-gateway choice. New test cases cover the direct-`-harness` craft + non-listed-agent forms. Also confirmed by a 5-turn live soak ($0.037): greeting/version/discovery/file-read all correct; the `.env` read was refused at the MODEL layer (the code deny-list path is unit-verified separately). Scope opinions noted (not bugs): finance-alpha/code-alpha should join PROTECTED_GATEWAY_AGENTS when they ship; sourcing the set from a routing.json \"daily-use\" flag is an M1 nicety.\n11\t\n12\t## 1. Verdict (original, pre-fix)\n13\t**NO.** The shipped harness does NOT genuinely uphold the 5 invariants. It contains critical P0 defects that break the bounded loop/ledger invariants (causing massive hidden double-billing) and violate the gateway regression acceptance gate.\n14\t\n15\t## 2. Defects (Reproduced & Verified)\n16\t\n17\t| Severity | Location | Defect | Repro / Consequence | Minimal Fix |\n18\t| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n19\t| **P0** | `clients.mjs:168` | **Unbounded Double-Billing on Stream Aborts** | **Repro:** A severed TCP connection or in-band SSE error occurs after 1000 tokens are streamed but before the final `message_delta` arrives. <br>**Consequence:** `output` tracks `obj.usage.output_tokens`, which Anthropic only sends at the end of the stream. Mid-stream, `output` is `0`. `classifyStreamFailure` sees `committedOutput === 0` and classifies it as `transient`. The harness retries up to 3 times, double-billing the input + generated tokens while the ledger silently records `0` output tokens. Breaks Invariant 3 & 4. | In the `catch (e)` block of `reasonAnthropic`, estimate the output tokens from the accumulated text length before building `partialUsage`: `const estOut = output || approxTokens(text); e.partialUsage = { ..., output: estOut }`. |\n20\t| **P0** | `sandbox-lab-gui/server.mjs:127` | **Gateway Non-Regression Failure** | **Repro:** Add `alpha-v0` to the `GWL_HARNESS_AGENTS` env var and launch the agent. <br>**Consequence:** `resolveHarnessCommand` blindly replaces `agent-chat-v0-gateway.mjs` with `agent-chat-v0-harness.mjs` if the ID is in the list, breaking the explicit acceptance gate requirement that `alpha-v0` *always* routes to the gateway regardless of the flag. | Add `if (agentId === 'alpha-v0') return cmd;` at the top of `resolveHarnessCommand` before checking `listed.includes()`. |\n21\t\n22\t*(Note: F6 provenance tightening (rejecting bare files like `makefile` when only an absolute path was seen) acts as a false-negative, but this is explicitly documented as deferred to M2 full-root resolution in the instructions. It is not flagged as a bug here.)*\n23\t\n24\t## 3. Unsubstantiated Claims\n25\t\n26\t*   **\"F7: severed TCP AFTER output -> fatal once\" & \"F4: in-band SSE error AFTER output -> fatal\"**: These claims are factually **FALSE**. Because Anthropic does not stream `output_tokens` incrementally during `content_block_delta`, the code's `output` variable remains `0` until the stream completes. Any error mid-stream is treated as \"0 committed output\" and retried infinitely up to the max-retry cap.\n27\t*   **Cost/Cache Claim (38% cheaper)**: This claim is mathematically sound for isolating the cache effect (it compares against the exact same small prefix size, not OpenClaw's 17.5k bloated prefix), but it is instantly wiped out by the P0 double-billing bug if the network stutters.\n28\t\n29\t## 4. Test Quality Assessment\n30\t\n31\tThe test suite provides a false sense of security regarding streaming failures. \n32\t*   **The Mocking Trap:** Tests like `clients-retry-1` (\"a fatal-after-output reason() books the partial COST\") pass **trivially**. The test runner uses a mock `reason()` function that manually throws an error with `.partialUsage.output = 100` already attached. It completely bypasses the real `reasonAnthropic` stream parser, blinding the test suite to the fact that the real parser fails to populate `output` mid-stream. The tests assert the *mock's* behavior, not the *client's* reality.\n33\t\n34\t## 5. Missed by Prior Swarms\n35\t\n36\t1.  **The Stream Token Accounting Gap:** None of the 4 agents in the previous swarms realized that Anthropic's SSE protocol defers the `usage.output_tokens` payload until the `message_delta` event at the very end of the stream. They trusted the code's `committedOutput > 0` logic without understanding the provider's wire format.\n37\t2.  **The Routing Leak:** The swarms focused intensely on the core harness logic (`loop.mjs`, `step.mjs`) but completely ignored the entry-point integration in `sandbox-lab-gui/server.mjs`, missing the critical `alpha-v0` routing leak.\n38\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01R7onNqhV8BYzhXq32rMA1B","session_id":"75eda862-34e1-4a42-a5f6-73eb4ef1cd9a","uuid":"bae9690d-93a8-4bc3-9696-6032f4c3a9db","timestamp":"2026-06-23T18:18:39.756Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Ground Gandalf diagnosis of Agentic-Home"}
