{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012eMf7sYXWfzWyXbH8Aqhzh","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# M0 VALIDATION & SWARM REVIEW REPORT — Sovereign t2r Harness\n2\t\n3\t**Date:** 2026-05-28 (supersedes the 2026-05-26 conceptual pre-build review; see §6)\n4\t**Target:** the shipped M0 at `gwl-t2r-brain/harness/*.mjs` + `sandbox-lab-gui/agent-chat-v0-harness.mjs` + `server.mjs` flag (commit `ca227113`).\n5\t**Method:** a **105-agent, 10-round swarm** (`gwl-t2r-brain/harness/.swarm-m0-validation.mjs`, 6.5M tokens, ~43 min) — 8 dimension reviewers + a prior-claim verifier → perspective-diverse adversarial verification (repro/scope/fix lenses, majority vote) → deep-think design panel → completeness critics (concurrency / Windows / adversarial / boundary) → synthesis + an independent skeptic challenge. **Grounded by independent repro scripts run by the orchestrator** for the load-bearing claims.\n6\t\n7\t---\n8\t\n9\t## 1. Executive Verdict\n10\t\n11\t**M0 is architecturally sound, but as originally shipped the acceptance gate did NOT cleanly hold.** Two reproducible bugs reachable through the shipped ecgberht pilot violated load-bearing invariants:\n12\t\n13\t- **F1 — a stalled SSE stream hung the loop forever** (broke invariant #3 *always bounded* AND #5 *always write accounting*: a hang never reaches `writeAccounting`).\n14\t- **F2 — the per-agent monthly wallet cap was silently not enforced** (the harness enforced the $100 default, not ecgberht's configured $30 — the banner displayed $30 but the loop allowed 3.3× that). The prior report missed this entirely.\n15\t\n16\t**Both are now fixed, tested, and re-validated** (this session). The remaining swarm findings are genuinely M1-hardening or contained edge cases. **One finding (F3) is a real but contained anti-fabrication gap whose safe fix is *not* the obvious one — it is proposed in §4 for a decision, not yet applied.**\n17\t\n18\t**What was verified to HOLD** (by reading + repro):\n19\t- **#1 byte-stable prefix / no mid-loop model swap:** holds. `freezePrefix` deep-freezes once; `assertPrefixStable` is an O(1) identity check; `buildPayload` asserts before every `reason()`. Live gate: prefix byte-identical across 4 calls, model locked, **one** `cache_creation`, hits 93%→77%.\n20\t- **#4 truthful ledger row matches the gateway reader:** holds. `writeTurnLedgerRow` emits `source:\"plugin-agent_end\"`, dedup-by-`turn_id`, `tokens.reasoning` split — byte-identical to what `readTurnRow` consumes.\n21\t- **#5 accounting always written:** holds on every exit path (refusal / abort / guard-stop / final) — and now also on the F1 stream-stall (the fatal error aborts *into* `writeAccounting`).\n22\t- Test gate: **harness 16/16, brain suite 61/61**; live gate **PASS** (39% cheaper than the uncached baseline).\n23\t\n24\t---\n25\t\n26\t## 2. Swarm Findings — verified, severity-ranked\n27\t\n28\tCounts: 37 raw → 22 deduped → **8 confirmed, 14 rescoped, 0 refuted-to-nothing**, + 15 completeness survivors. Adjudicated below (orchestrator's call after weighing synthesis vs. skeptic + own repro).\n29\t\n30\t| # | Finding | Sev | Disposition | File:line |\n31\t|---|---------|-----|-------------|-----------|\n32\t| **F1** | **Stalled SSE body read hangs the loop forever** — fetch timeout cleared at header resolution; body read unbounded. Repro: hung >2.5s, no abort, no accounting. | **P1** | **FIXED (M0)** | `clients.mjs` |\n33\t| **F2** | **Wallet cap not threaded** — `runLoop` called with no `walletConfig` → `checkMonthSpend` uses $100 default, not ecgberht's $30. Banner lies. | **P1** | **FIXED (M0)** | `agent-chat-v0-harness.mjs:259` |\n34\t| **F3** | **Bare filenames bypass provenance** — `Makefile`/`Dockerfile`/`.env`/`LICENSE` (no slash, no ≤7-char ext) aren't classified as locators → not checked, not added to `seenLocators`. False-NEGATIVE. | **P2** | **PROPOSED (§4)** | `step.mjs:64,90` |\n35\t| F4 | In-band Anthropic SSE `error` event (overloaded/api_error) swallowed → silent no-op turn, burns empty billed calls. | P2 | M1 | `clients.mjs:151-163` |\n36\t| F5 | `checkGuards` fails OPEN if a `bounds` field is missing (`>= undefined` → false). Unreachable via the pilot (`loopBounds()` always complete). | P2 | M1 | `loop.mjs:70-77` |\n37\t| F6 | Basename suffix can resolve to a *different* same-named file than the seen deep path (needs a collision). | P2 | M1 | `step.mjs:113-129` |\n38\t| F7 | Severed TCP mid-stream raised inside `reasonAnthropic` (outside `fetchWithRetry`) → no backoff. | P2 | M1 | `clients.mjs` |\n39\t| F8 | A 120s abort re-sends a billable generation POST up to 3× (non-idempotent). | P3 | M1 | `clients.mjs:79` |\n40\t| F9 | Final SSE line w/o trailing `\\n` dropped → output-token undercount. | P3 | M1 | `clients.mjs` |\n41\t| F10 | `normLoc` lowercasing merges distinct files on a case-sensitive root (harmless on the Windows pilot host). | P3 | M1 | `step.mjs:39` |\n42\t| F11 | Transient MCP startup failure permanently disables tools for the session (no retry). | P3 | M1 | `agent-chat-v0-harness.mjs` |\n43\t| C-inj | **Prompt-injection in a tool observation can fabricate a locator into `seenLocators`**, defeating provenance on a later step. | P1→M1 | M1 (see §4 note) | `step.mjs` extractLocators |\n44\t| C-parse | A *leading* JSON object (non-decision) before the real decision makes `parseDecision` return null → wasted step. | P1→M1 | M1 | `step.mjs` parseDecision |\n45\t| C-final | `final_answer` with no `answer` field returns raw decision JSON; an object answer → `[object Object]`. | P2 | M1 | `step.mjs:147` |\n46\t| C-xwin | Two concurrent harness windows for one agent can misattribute per-turn cost (`waitForTurnRow` matches by agent+ts, not turn_id). | P2 | M1 | `agent-chat-v0-harness.mjs` |\n47\t| C-proj | `/project` switch can race the next message (old `fsTool` nulled mid-flight). Mitigated by the `busy` gate; narrow window. | P2 | M1 | `agent-chat-v0-harness.mjs` |\n48\t\n49\t**Correctly deferred / not-a-bug** (do not flag): `read_raw`, MCP supervisor/restart, Hybrid Pre-Summary Router + Local MoE, episodic/semantic memory, cache-warmth promoter (seam reserved), resume/hydration reference-heal (M0 has no resume executor — YAGNI by design; the prior report's \"Hydration Trap\" is a non-issue).\n50\t\n51\t---\n52\t\n53\t## 3. Changes APPLIED this session (the two agreed must-fixes)\n54\t\n55\tBoth the synthesizer and the independent skeptic agreed these are true M0 correctness/safety bugs; the orchestrator independently reproduced both.\n56\t\n57\t1. **F1 — stream idle-timeout (`clients.mjs`).** Added `withDeadline()` wrapping every SSE `reader.read()` (and the Ollama/Google `.json()` body reads) with a per-chunk-reset deadline (`GWL_STREAM_IDLE_MS`, default 90s). On stall it cancels the reader and rejects with a **fatal (non-retryable)** error that propagates to the loop's `catch` → `writeAccounting` — restoring *both* the bounded-loop and always-accounting invariants. (Per the skeptic: the abort is terminal, so a half-streamed generation is never re-billed.)\n58\t2. **F2 — thread the wallet cap.** Added `walletConfig(agentEntry)` to `config.mjs` (derives `{monthlyWalletUsd, softAlertUsd}` from routing fields) and passed it into the entry's `runLoop({...})`. The pilot now enforces ecgberht's $30, matching the banner.\n59\t\n60\t**Tests added (the test gap that let F2 ship is now closed):** F1 stall→fatal-abort, F1 fatal-error→abort-still-writes-accounting, `walletConfig` derivation, and **enforced-cap-equals-configured-cap threaded into `checkMonthSpend`**. Harness suite **12 → 16 green**; brain suite **61/61**; live gate still **PASS** (real streaming unaffected by `withDeadline`).\n61\t\n62\t---\n63\t\n64\t## 4. F3 (bare-filename provenance) — RESOLVED: Option B applied\n65\t\n66\t**Decision (2026-05-28): Option B.** A code-owned **sensitive-file deny-list** was added to `step.mjs` (`SENSITIVE_FILE_RE` + `scanSensitive`, applied to content-reading/non-discovery tools, taking precedence over provenance): reads of `.env`/`.env.*`/`auth-profiles.json`/`*.key`/`*.pem`/`*.p12`/`*.pfx`/`*.ppk`/`*.keystore`/`*.kdbx`/`id_rsa*`/`id_ed25519*`/`id_dsa*`/`.npmrc`/`.netrc`/`credentials*`/`secrets*` are refused outright, regardless of whether the locator was \"seen.\" This is **additive** (anti-EXFILTRATION; can only reject, never loosen provenance's anti-FABRICATION) and closes the only real leak vector (the workspace `.env` reachable under the pilot's default tool root). Tested: `isSensitivePath` recognition + an end-to-end \"read `.env` is DENIED even when seeded into `seenLocators`\" test. The **general bare-filename tokenizer fix is deferred to M1** (the synthesizer's widen-`extractLocators` proposal was rejected as too risky — it would loosen the suffix rule).\n67\t\n68\t---\n69\t\n70\t### (original options, for the record)\n71\t\n72\t## 4-orig. PROPOSED change for decision — F3 (bare-filename provenance)\n73\t\n74\t**The disagreement.** The synthesizer rated F3 P1-fix-now and proposed widening `extractLocators`/`paramLocators` to treat any ≥3-char token as a locator. The skeptic rated it **P2-defer** and showed the proposed fix is *risky*: widening `extractLocators` adds every prose word (`README`, `Error`, `function`) to `seenLocators`, which **loosens the suffix rule and can re-open a fabrication path** — worse than the bug.\n75\t\n76\t**Orchestrator's adjudication.** The skeptic is right about the fix risk; do **not** widen the tokenizer under M0's frozen mandate. But one fact both under-weighted: the pilot's default tool root is the **workspace root**, which contains `.env` (real API keys), and `.env` bypasses the locator classifier — so the contained-ness depends on tool-root scoping. The genuine residual risk is *reading an un-discovered sensitive bare file within the root*.\n77\t\n78\t**Recommendation (pick one):**\n79\t- **Option A (skeptic): defer F3 entirely to M1.** Rationale: the MCP server's root-scoping is the real containment boundary; exploiting it needs the model to *choose* to read an in-root file it never saw, and the pilot is off-by-default. Do the tokenizer fix properly in M1 (filename-shaped heuristic + tests).\n80\t- **Option B (recommended): defer the tokenizer to M1, but add a tiny sensitive-file deny-list NOW.** ~10 additive lines in the `runTool` path: always reject reads of `.env`, `auth-profiles.json`, `*.key`, `*.pem`, `id_rsa*`, `*.secret*`, regardless of provenance. This is *additive* (can only reject, never loosen), touches nothing frozen, and closes the only real leak vector (API keys). Lowest risk for the most relevant harm.\n81\t\n82\t**Related M1 note (C-inj):** the same `seenLocators`-growth path means a prompt-injection embedded in a *tool observation* can fabricate a locator that later passes provenance. This is the deeper version of F3 and is M1 (it needs a trust boundary on observation-derived locators). Flagged so it isn't lost.\n83\t\n84\t---\n85\t\n86\t## 5. The full M1 hardening backlog (from this swarm)\n87\t\n88\tStreaming resilience: F4 (in-band SSE error → transient retry), F7 (mid-stream TCP → backoff), F8 (no-retry on generation abort / idempotency key), F9 (flush residual buffer). Provenance: F3 tokenizer (filename-shaped), F6 (absolute-resolve before compare), C-inj (observation-locator trust boundary), F10 (case-sensitivity opt-in). Robustness: F5 (normalize/validate `bounds` at `runLoop` entry — defend the primitive), F11 + MCP supervisor/restart + `callTool` timeout tightening, C-parse (iterate balanced JSON objects), C-final (validate `final_answer.answer`), C-proj (guard `/project` with `busy`), C-xwin (match the ledger row by `turn_id`, not agent+ts). Plus the pre-planned M1: `read_raw`, moving history breakpoint, Hybrid Pre-Summary compression, confidence-gated flash, episodic memory, warmth promoter.\n89\t\n90\t---\n91\t\n92\t## 6. The prior (2026-05-26) report — right vs wrong\n93\t\n94\t**Right:** flagged the streaming-timeout-cleared-at-headers bug (= F1, the most serious), the bare-`Makefile` provenance blindspot (= F3), and correctly scoped the MCP supervisor / `read_raw` / Hybrid Router / resume as M1.\n95\t\n96\t**Wrong / missed:**\n97\t- **Over-optimistic verdict** (\"a resounding success… clear to proceed to M1\"). It filed F1 and F3 as *M1 hardening*; F1 is an M0 invariant violation.\n98\t- **Missed F2 entirely** — the most user-visible safety defect (3.3× overspend on the pilot, with a lying banner).\n99\t- **Missed F4** (the concrete transient-overload failure mechanism).\n100\t- **Unverified cost claim** (\"38% reduction\") — no substantiating artifact on the M0 path; treat as carried over from a sim. (This session measured **34–39%** vs the uncached baseline on the live gate — directionally consistent, now actually measured.)\n101\t- Its \"Hydration Trap\" (A1) is not an M0 issue — M0 has no resume executor.\n102\t\n103\t---\n104\t\n105\t## 7. Bottom line\n106\t\n107\tThe M0 design is correct and the gate now **genuinely holds** after F1 + F2 (applied + tested + live-verified this session). F3 is real but contained — **decide Option A vs B in §4 before it ships to anyone beyond the off-by-default pilot.** Everything else is a well-characterized M1 backlog. The harness is clear to proceed to M1 once F3 is dispositioned.\n108\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01R7onNqhV8BYzhXq32rMA1B","session_id":"75eda862-34e1-4a42-a5f6-73eb4ef1cd9a","uuid":"df6c3e8d-b7c5-41d6-ba7e-0da358c97a7e","timestamp":"2026-06-23T18:18:40.017Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Ground Gandalf diagnosis of Agentic-Home"}
