{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01R7onNqhV8BYzhXq32rMA1B","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect. Now I have all the evidence I need. Let me compile my findings:\n\n## FINDINGS REPORT: Ground-Truth Analysis of Architectural Surface Area vs. Daily Use\n\n---\n\n### 1. DEFAULT-OFF / NOT-WIRED INVENTORY\n\n**Finding:** Extensive flag-gated feature surface; mixed wiring status.\n\nThe harness (GWL t2r) implements 6 waves of default-OFF capability:\n- **Wave 1 (C2 Clarify):** `GWL_HARNESS_CLARIFY` flag gates the `ask` terminal action — **not wired to daily vehicle** (alpha-v0 flow does not call this flag)\n- **Wave 2 (C3 Progress):** `GWL_HARNESS_PROGRESS` flag gates per-observe status narration — **not wired to daily vehicle**\n- **Wave 3 (C2b Approval):** `GWL_HARNESS_APPROVAL` flag gates tool approval gates — **not wired to daily vehicle**\n- **Wave 4 (C6a Verify):** `GWL_HARNESS_VERIFY` flag gates read-only verification worker — **not wired to daily vehicle**\n- **Wave 5 (Replan):** `GWL_HARNESS_REPLAN` flag gates outer-loop strategy reset (explicitly noted: \"**not yet wired to an entrypoint**\") — **aspirational**\n- **Wave 6 (C6b Command verify):** `GWL_HARNESS_VERIFY` + `GWL_HARNESS_APPROVAL` together; both **not wired to daily vehicle**\n\n**Evidence:**\n- `C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home\\plans\\foreman\\gwl-harness-orchestration\\EXECUTION-LOG.md:35` — Wave 5 explicitly states \"plumbing-ready, like W3/W4\"\n- `C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home\\plans\\foreman\\gwl-harness-orchestration\\EXECUTION-LOG.md:47` — Project shipped with \"6 contiguous waves, each default-OFF + flag/callback-gated\"\n- No grep matches for these flags in the alpha-v0 daily dispatcher\n\n**Conclusion:** ~6 waves of capability exist at feature-complete granularity, all default-OFF, none routed into the daily alpha-v0 dispatcher. The harness is **foundational but not yet integrated into daily vehicle flow**.\n\n---\n\n### 2. DAILY-USAGE EVIDENCE\n\n**Finding:** Limited, sporadic alpha-v0 usage; logs exist but show low volume and long gaps.\n\n**Evidence of use:**\n- `C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home\\logs\\agents\\alpha-v0\\signals.jsonl` contains 20 lines (sampled May 16, May 20, May 23 — **3 dates in ~6 days, then silent** until end of file)\n- Log entries show real provider calls (Gemini, Anthropic models) with cost tracking\n- Entries date-stamped 2026-05-16 to 2026-05-23 (last entry ~May 23, now at 2026-06-23 — **one-month gap with no new entries**)\n\n**Evidence of non-use:**\n- `.alpha` directory is **empty** (`C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home\\.alpha` has no subdirectories or transcript files)\n- `logs/agents/alpha-v0/signals.jsonl` has **20 records over 8 days, then silent for 30+ days**\n- No transcript accumulation in `.alpha/` (the documented per-project transcript location)\n- Cost signals show \"no verifier wired yet\" on every outcome\n\n**Conclusion:** Alpha-v0 was **tested/piloted during dev (May 15-23)**, then **abandoned as daily vehicle**. Usage is **designed but not actually evidenced post-May-23**. The system is architecturally ready for daily use but **not deployed to actually be the daily driver**.\n\n---\n\n### 3. PLAN/DOC SPRAWL\n\n**Finding:** Substantial doc inventory; 3 active Foreman handoff plans; multi-version architecture.\n\n**Markdown inventory:**\n- **Root level:** 137 markdown files (confirmed via `find ... *.md`)\n- **`docs/` subtree:** 196 markdown files\n- **Total:** ~330+ markdown files across the repo\n\n**Foreman handoff plans (active, sequenced):**\n1. `C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home\\plans\\foreman\\gwl-harness-orchestration\\` — **GREEN (2026-06-12)**, 6 waves, 367 tests\n2. `C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home\\plans\\foreman\\t2r-brain\\` — **GREEN (2026-06-10)**, 7 waves, 263 tests\n3. `C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home\\plans\\foreman\\t2r-harness-to-GA\\` — **GREEN (2026-06-10)**, 8 waves, 154 tests\n\nEach contains DESCRIPTION, IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN, EXECUTION-LOG, plus `.foreman/` subdirectory with checkpoint state.\n\n**Version scheme complexity:**\n- **System version:** `v<BRAIN>.<HARNESS>` (current `v2.1` = gen-2 brain + gen-1 harness)\n- **Agent maturity ladder:** v0–v1–v2 (alpha-v0 is v0-stage agent running v2.1 system)\n- **Brain generations:** v0 (baseline Opus), v1 (dynamic-context t2r), v2 (reasoning-agent with LoRA), v3 (two-brain LoRA students)\n- **Harness generations:** M0 (shipped w/ P0 bugs), M1 (hardening plan), Phase A–D, Phase E–F (sequenced)\n- **Wave numbering:** 6 waves (harness orchestration), 7 waves (t2r brain), 8 waves (harness-to-GA)\n\n**Evidence:**\n- `C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home\\CLAUDE.md:15-17` — explicit version scheme explanation\n- `C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home\\ARCHITECTURE-Reasoning-Agent-v3.md` — separate v3 architecture for two-brain distillation\n- `C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home\\plans\\foreman\\` — three independent handoff dirs\n\n**Conclusion:** ~13+ distinct planning/architecture docs at root + docs/ (counting major versions + phase plans). Version multiplication (v0-v1-v2 ladder × system v2.1 × brain generations × harness generations × Phase A-F) creates a **complex conceptual surface that rivals the code complexity**. Plans are **sequenced and actively executed** (not abandoned), but the **sheer number of moving versions** creates cognitive overhead.\n\n---\n\n### 4. COST-THESIS / VALIDATION\n\n**Finding:** Cost claims are documented but NOT validated against real provider invoices; all validation is internal self-report.\n\n**No evidence of external cost validation:**\n- Searched for \"invoice\", \"ground truth\", \"validated against\", \"actual bill\", \"provider invoice\" — **no matches found**\n- Cost tracking is entirely gateway-internal (`~/openclaw/usage.jsonl`) and self-reported\n\n**Cost evidence:**\n- `C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home\\Sandbox Setup Package\\COSTS.md` — comprehensive budgeting doc but all numbers are **internal projections** (\"~$15 / million tokens per Opus\", \"rough Apr 2026 prices\")\n- `C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home\\docs\\session-logs\\SESSION-LOG-2026-05-25-t2r-tiering-cost-MTD.md` — cost tracking but against **gateway's own self-report**, not Anthropic's dashboard\n- Pricing doc notes correction: `C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home\\CLAUDE_hist.md` — Aurora's pricing collector was **wrong for weeks** (pinned deprecated Opus 4.1 $15/$75 instead of current 4.7 $5/$25), only discovered via docstring-scraping, not via invoice reconciliation\n\n**Brain-agnostic claim (verified):**\n- `C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home\\plans\\foreman\\t2r-brain\\IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md:17-18` — **\"The seam is model-size-agnostic (D9): swapping a bigger model into any stage (7–8B → 70B-class → 671B-class as hardware allows) is a CONFIG change, not a re-architecture.\"**\n- `C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home\\plans\\foreman\\t2r-brain\\EXECUTION-LOG.md:60` — \"the t2r brain is built and **three-way A/B-measured** ... on the **one pinned, brain-agnostic harness**\"\n- Evidence: Wave 7 (eval-ab.mjs) ran the same harness against **Opus-4.8 baseline** + **t2r** + **Sovereign qwen2.5:7b** — all three used identical `pickLock`/`reason`/`compress` seams, only model swapped\n\n**Conclusion:** The harness is genuinely **brain-agnostic** (model pluggable via config). **Cost thesis is not validated against real provider invoices** — it is self-reported by the gateway. Pricing was discovered to be wrong (Aurora bug) only through code-scraping, not invoice audit. No evidence of ground-truth cost reconciliation.\n\n---\n\n### 5. CORPUS REALITY\n\n**Finding:** Corpus apparatus is aspirational; no evidence of real accumulation.\n\n**No user-profile corpus found:**\n- `C:\\Users\\john\\gwl-corpus\\` — **outside the workspace, inaccessible to this read-only scan**; documented in `.gitignore` as reserved\n- **No in-repo corpus location** identified via grep/glob\n\n**Training apparatus status:**\n- `C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home\\CLAUDE.md:256` — Documents the corpus path as **\"user-profile training-data root (formerly ~/gbrain/, renamed 2026-05-15)\"** — implies *planned* but **doesn't confirm actual data accumulation**\n- Training-capture is **wave-complete but not live-wired**: `C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home\\plans\\foreman\\t2r-brain\\EXECUTION-LOG.md:42-47` — Wave 6 \"Training-data capture\" is built and tested; the log states **\"Capture-only — no training/distill/LoRA\"** and **\"no existing source modified\"**\n\n**LoRA status:**\n- Documented in multiple architecture files as Phase C / Phase F future work\n- No evidence of actual LoRA weights, checkpoints, or training runs\n- `C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home\\CLAUDE.md:11` — References RTX 4070 as unblocking \"Phase C of Wave 7 — specifically the G-32 LoRA activation\", indicating LoRA is **still aspirational**\n\n**Conclusion:** The corpus and LoRA training apparatus are **fully designed, partially implemented (capture path built), but not actually running**. No evidence of real tuples accumulating or LoRA weights being trained. The apparatus is **foundational/aspirational, not operational**.\n\n---\n\n### 6. AI-REVIEWS-AI: SAME-FAMILY BLIND SPOTS\n\n**Finding:** Quality loops are same-model-family; independent review caught 2 P0 bugs all same-family swarms missed.\n\n**QA loops identified (Swarm Sandwich):**\n- **Design swarm** → **Solo build** → **Validation swarm** (per `C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home\\CLAUDE.md:19` and `expert-coder/SKILL.md`)\n- All three swarms run same-family models (Anthropic agents in most cases)\n\n**Two P0s all swarms missed (independent review caught):**\n- `C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home\\docs\\reports\\REPORT-INDEPENDENT-VALIDATION.md:4-8`:\n  - **P0-1 — Unbounded Double-Billing on Stream Aborts** (`clients.mjs:168`): Mid-stream TCP severance after tokens streamed but before final `message_delta` would trigger retries (up to 3×) while ledger recorded $0. The prior swarms trusted the code's `committedOutput > 0` logic without understanding Anthropic's SSE protocol defers `usage.output_tokens` to the end.\n  - **P0-2 — Gateway Non-Regression Failure** (`server.mjs:127`): `alpha-v0` could