nal | Foundational, not operational |\n| **QA loop blindness** | 2 P0s caught by independent review that same-family swarms all missed | Same-family loops have correlated blind spots; independence helps |\n\n**Central thesis CONFIRMED:** The built/planned architectural surface area is significantly outrunning validated daily use and independent verification. The system is feature-complete at a design level but not integrated, deployed, or tested end-to-end in a real daily-use scenario."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"75eda862-34e1-4a42-a5f6-73eb4ef1cd9a","uuid":"4335b74e-6eb8-456b-b0f0-018659c218ce","timestamp":"2026-06-23T18:19:26.214Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I'm running a deep-think advisory analysis of the C:\\dev\\Agentic-Home project (a solo, non-technical user's AI-agent research sandbox: a Next.js GUI, the OpenClaw runtime, a custom cost-optimizing \"t2r/t2rs\" brain+harness, LoRA-training ambitions on an RTX 4070, and meta-tooling skills Crucible/Foreman/researchPrime/Gandalf). I need CURRENT ground-truth on ONE central thesis: that built/planned architectural surface area is outrunning validated daily use and independent verification. Be very thorough but report only conclusions + evidence (file:line), not file dumps.\n\nFind and report concisely on:\n\n1. DEFAULT-OFF / NOT-WIRED INVENTORY: How many features/waves are flagged default-OFF or \"not yet wired to daily vehicle\"? Look at the recent harness work (search for env flags like GWL_*, \"default-OFF\", \"default OFF\", \"not yet wired\", flag-gated). List the flags and whether any are documented as actually armed/used in daily flow.\n\n2. DAILY-USAGE EVIDENCE: Is there ANY telemetry/log showing alpha-v0 (the supposed daily-driver agent) is actually used day-to-day? Check logs/agents/*.jsonl existence/recency, any usage counters, transcripts under .alpha/. Report whether real recurring daily use is evidenced or just designed.\n\n3. PLAN/DOC SPRAWL: Count markdown